      "sourceText": "おかげで (JLPT N3) | Bunpro\nLoading user data...\nBunpro\nGrammar Info\nN3 Lesson 2: 20/22\nお\n陰\n(\nかげ\n)\nで\nThanks to, Because of\nDetails\nExamples\nResources\nおかげで\nThanks to, Because of\nDetails\nExamples\nResources\nDetails\nExamples\nResources\nReady to transform your studies?\nLearn N5 in under a month!\nTry now, no credit card required!\nTry Bunpro\nLearn More\nStructure\nVerb +\nおかげ\nで\n［い］Adjective\n+\nおかげ\nで\n［な］Adjective +\nな\n+\nおかげ\nで\nNoun +\nの\n+\nおかげ\nで\nDetails\nRegister\nStandard\nAbout おかげで\nEnglish\nJapanese\nおかげで\n(or お\n陰\n(\nかげ\n)\nで in kanji) is an expression that is used to show thanks or appreciation in Japanese. It is usually translated simply as 'thanks to (A)', or 'because of (A)'.\nおかげで\nis a combination of the polite\nprefix\nお, the\nnoun\n陰\n(\nかげ\n)\n'shade', and the\ncase marking particle\nで.\nおかげで can be used after any word in its\nattributive form\n.\nLiterally,\nお\n陰\n(\nかげ\n)\nで\nmeans 'in the shade of (A)'. This implies that (B) was only made possible due to (A) creating the ideal situation for it to occur.\nCaution\nおかげで may sometimes be used sarcastically, in the same way as 'thanks to (A)' in English. In these sentences, it is usually quite clear from the context/tone of voice that the actual meaning is negative.\nFun Fact\nおかげで is often used at the beginning of a sentence in the same way as 'thankfully' or 'luckily' in English. This just means that whatever comes after おかげで happened, despite negative outcomes also being possible.\nRelated\nExpand All\nせいで\nBecause of, Due to, Blame\nN3 Grammar\nBoth mean 'because of', but with opposite tone. おかげで expresses a thankful cause, e.g. 先生のおかげで合格できた ('Thanks to my teacher, I passed.') せいで places blame for something negative, e.g. 雨のせいで試合が中止になった ('The game was canceled because of the rain.')\nために\nために\nDue to, Because of, As a result of\nN3 Grammar\nために and せいで can both express the idea of 'due to (A)', but they differ in that おかげで almost always describes a desirable result, while ために can be used with either a positive or negative nuance. ために can also, in some cases, mean 'for the purpose of (A)', while おかげで cannot be used in this way.\nそのため(に)\nそのために\nFor that reason, Because of that, To that end\nN3 Grammar\nBoth express cause and effect, but with different tone and usage. おかげで implies a positive result and gratitude, e.g. 先生のおかげで合格できた ('Thanks to my teacher, I passed.') そのため(に) is neutral, objective, and often appears at the start of a sentence. It can also mean 'for that purpose'.\nにつき\nにつき\nDue to, On account of, Each or every\nN2 Grammar\nBoth express cause, but differ in tone and formality. おかげで implies a positive result with gratitude, e.g. 先生のおかげで合格できました ('Thanks to my teacher, I passed.') につき states a neutral reason, often used in formal notices, e.g. 雨天につき中止します ('Due to rain, it is canceled.') It also only follows nouns.\nVocab Coverage\nAll Bunpro Vocab that appears on this item.\nExpand List\nKnowledge Check\nExamples\n--:--\nSentence\nTranslation\n薬\n(\nくすり\n)\nのお\n陰\n(\nかげ\n)\nで\nだいぶよくなりました。\nThanks to\nthe medicine, I got much better.\n風\n(\nかぜ\n)\nが\n強\n(\nつよ\n)\nい\nお\n陰\n(\nかげ\n)\nで\n、ヨットのスピードが\n上\n(\nあ\n)\nがった。\nThanks to\nthe strong wind, the yacht gained speed.\nお\n陰\n(\nかげ\n)\nで\n助\n(\nたす\n)\nかったよ。\n来\n(\nき\n)\nてくれてありがとう。\nThanks to\nyou, I was saved. Thank you for coming.\nスマホ\nのお\n陰\n(\nかげ\n)\nで\n、\n目的地\n(\nもくてきち\n)\nにスムーズに\n着\n(\nつ\n)\nきました。\nThanks to\nmy smartphone, I had no trouble arriving at my destination.\n君\n(\nきみ\n)\nのお\n陰\n(\nかげ\n)\nで\n取引\n(\nとりひき\n)\nは\n失敗\n(\nしっぱい\n)\nだったよ。\nThanks to\nyou the deal was a failure!\nGet more example sentences!\nPremium users get access to 12 example sentences on all Grammar Points.\nTry Bunpro\nSelf-Study Sentences\nStudy your own way!\nAdd sentences and study them alongside Bunpro sentences.\nTry Bunpro\nOnline\nおかげさまで [video]\nMiku Real Japanese\nOffline\n[AIAIJ] An Integrated Approach to Intermediate Japanese\nPage 228\nGenki II 3rd Edition\nPage 139\nTobira\nPage 195\nTobira\nPage 71\nTrack Resources!\nBunpro tracks all of the resources you’ve visited, and offers relevant bookmarks of physical books to help with offline tracking.\nTry Bunpro\nおかげで – Grammar Discussion\nMost Recent Replies (14 in total)\nIsurandil492\n文プロのお陰で文法を理解できるようになってきた。\nThanks to\nBunpro, I am starting to understand grammar.\nConsidering it’s なって\nきた\nshouldn’t it be\nThanks to\nBunpro, I started understanding/to understand grammar.\n?\nSometimes, I have the feeling that I am stricter in translating than would be appropriate in Japanese  Probably, that just shows that I am still learning how to do this properly\ndarzington\nI’m wondering the same thing!\nusername2\nGot questions about おかげで?\nJoin us to discuss, ask, and learn together!\nJoin the Discussion\nBunpro\nSimplifying Japanese\nOfficial Apps\nLearn More\nJoin us!\nCompany\nNews\nCareers\nAbout Us\nTestimonials\nAcknowledgements\nFor Teachers\nJapanese\nOfficial Forums\nContent Search\nReading Practice\nGrammar Library\nHiragana & Katakana\nSupport\nContact Us\nSupport & FAQ\n© 2026, Bunpro SRS.\nRead our\nTerms of Service\n,\nPrivacy Policy\nand\nCompany Overview\n.\nMade with\n❤️\nfrom Osaka.\nEnglish",
