      "sourceText": "がち (JLPT N3) | Bunpro\nLoading user data...\nBunpro\nGrammar Info\nN3 Lesson 10: 7/20\nがち\nApt to do, Tend to do, Prone to do\nDetails\nExamples\nResources\nがち\nApt to do, Tend to do, Prone to do\nDetails\nExamples\nResources\nDetails\nExamples\nResources\nReady to transform your studies?\nLearn N5 in under a month!\nTry now, no credit card required!\nTry Bunpro\nLearn More\nStructure\nVerb［stem］\n+\nがち\nNoun +\nがち\nNoun\n(1)\n+\nがち\n+\nな\n(2)\n+ Noun\n(1)\nVerb［stem］\n(2)\nの\nDetails\nRegister\nStandard\nRare Kanji\n勝ち\nAbout がち\nEnglish\nJapanese\nがち\nis a\nsuffix\nin Japanese that will be used after nouns, or the\nconjunctive form\nof verbs. It conveys that someone is 'apt to (A)', 'tends to (A)', or 'is prone to (A)'. Although not always negative,\nがち\nis most frequently used to express negative tendencies.\nFun Fact\nがち\nas a grammar structure comes from the word\n勝\n(\nが\n)\nち, meaning 'a win'.\n勝\n(\nが\n)\nち in itself is used to express something that appears 'repeatedly', or 'again and again'. Due to this,\nがち\nmay be thought of as similar to 'to win out' in English, meaning that 'although there are many possibilities, (A) winning out is the most likely'. This 'winning out' may be due to preference, or sheer good/bad luck.\nRelated\nExpand All\nっぽい\n-ish, -like, Characteristic of, Typical of, Tendency to\nN3 Grammar\nBoth がち and っぽい describe tendencies or characteristic qualities, but differ in nuance. がち is neutral and used for tendencies that happen often, e.g. つい忘れがちだ ('I tend to forget.'). っぽい expresses an inherent quality or the appearance of something, similar to the English '~ish', e.g. 子供っぽい性格 ('a childish personality').\nきらいがある\nきらいがある\nHave a tendency to, Tend to, Be slightly~\nN1 Grammar\nBoth express tendencies or patterns of behavior, but they differ in tone and usage. がち attaches to verb stems, and is neutral, used for tendencies that happen often, e.g. つい忘れがちだ ('I tend to forget.'). きらいがある follows the plain form of verbs and is typically used only for undesirable tendencies. Unlike がち, it can also express a tendency to not do something, e.g. 人の話を聞かないきらいがある ('He tends to not listen to others.').\nVocab Coverage\nAll Bunpro Vocab that appears on this item.\nExpand List\nKnowledge Check\nExamples\n--:--\nSentence\nTranslation\nそれは\n初心者\n(\nしょしんしゃ\n)\nに\nありがち\nのミスですね。\nThat is a mistake beginners\ntend to\nmake.\n彼\n(\nかれ\n)\nはいつも\n遠慮\n(\nえんりょ\n)\nがち\nだ。\nHe always\ntends to\nhold back.\n私\n(\nわたし\n)\nの\n息子\n(\nむすこ\n)\nは\n病気\n(\nびょうき\n)\nがち\nだ。\nMy boy is\napt to\nget sick.\nあの\n人\n(\nひと\n)\nはすぐ、\n痩\n(\nや\n)\nせることを\n諦\n(\nあきら\n)\nめがち\nだ。\nThat person is\nprone to\nquickly give up on losing weight.\n私\n(\nわたし\n)\nは\n昔\n(\nむかし\n)\nから\n遅刻\n(\nちこく\n)\nしがち\nだ。\nI have always been\nprone to\nbeing late.\nGet more example sentences!\nPremium users get access to 12 example sentences on all Grammar Points.\nTry Bunpro\nSelf-Study Sentences\nStudy your own way!\nAdd sentences and study them alongside Bunpro sentences.\nTry Bunpro\nOnline\nExpressing tendencies in Japanese\nTae Kim\nHow to use がち and ぎみ\nMaggie Sensei\nOffline\n[AIAIJ] An Integrated Approach to Intermediate Japanese\nPage 230\nTae Kim's Japanese Grammar Guide\nPage 328\nTrack Resources!\nBunpro tracks all of the resources you’ve visited, and offers relevant bookmarks of physical books to help with offline tracking.\nTry Bunpro\nがち – Grammar Discussion\nMost Recent Replies (3 in total)\nMZa\nI’ve found this can be written 勝ち  (very useful to retain this imho). Is it often written in kanji?\nDue to the kanji meaning ‘victory, prevail’ and the point being used for negative tendencies, i guess this implies that this point literally means something like ‘the negative tendencies win, prevail’, but how do we have to understand it syntactically (is it the stem of 勝つ used as a noun ?)?\nPep95\nMZa:\n勝ち\nOh nice! This will help a lot\nDaru\nMZa:\n'the negative tendencies win, prevail’, but how do we have to understand it syntactically (is it the stem of 勝つ used as a noun\nThat is exactly right! I didn’t know this myself, thank you for pointing it out!\nGot questions about がち?\nJoin us to discuss, ask, and learn together!\nJoin the Discussion\nBunpro\nSimplifying Japanese\nOfficial Apps\nLearn More\nJoin us!\nCompany\nNews\nCareers\nAbout Us\nTestimonials\nAcknowledgements\nFor Teachers\nJapanese\nOfficial Forums\nContent Search\nReading Practice\nGrammar Library\nHiragana & Katakana\nSupport\nContact Us\nSupport & FAQ\n© 2026, Bunpro SRS.\nRead our\nTerms of Service\n,\nPrivacy Policy\nand\nCompany Overview\n.\nMade with\n❤️\nfrom Osaka.\nEnglish",
