      "sourceText": "にすぎない (JLPT N2) | Bunpro\nLoading user data...\nBunpro\nGrammar Info\nN2 Lesson 9: 25/26\nに\n過\n(\nす\n)\nぎない\nNo more than, Just, Merely\nDetails\nExamples\nResources\nにすぎない\nNo more than, Just, Merely\nDetails\nExamples\nResources\nDetails\nExamples\nResources\nReady to transform your studies?\nLearn N5 in under a month!\nTry now, no credit card required!\nTry Bunpro\nLearn More\nStructure\nStandard\nPolite\nVerb +（\nだけ\n）\nにすぎない\n［い］Adjective\n+（\nだけ\n）\nにすぎない\n［な］Adjective\n+（\nな\nだけ\n）\nにすぎない\nNoun +（\nだけ\n）\nにすぎない\nDetails\nRegister\nFormal\nAbout にすぎない\nEnglish\nJapanese\nにすぎない\nis a common structure in Japanese used for indicating that something is 'no more than (A)', or 'merely (A)'. This expression is constructed from に, and the negated form of the る-Verb\n過\n(\nす\n)\nぎる, meaning 'to exceed', or 'to be more than'. Due to this, the literal translation of 'to not be more than (A)' reflects the English interpretations closely.\nにすぎない\nis slightly formal, but is heard fairly often in day-to-day speech as well. This grammar pattern may be used after verbs in any of their standard forms, い-Adjectives, な-Adjectives, or nouns.\nにすぎない\nis often seen paired with structures that will emphasize the phrase even further, such as ただ 'merely' or だけ 'just'. In the case of だけ, it will come between the target word and にすぎない. Also, standard conjugation rules will need to be remembered, such as adding な after a な-Adjective before だけ.\nFun-fact\nにすぎない\nmay occasionally appear in set phrases, such as\n氷山\n(\nひょうざん\n)\nの\n一角\n(\nいっかく\n)\nにすぎない\n, which means 'to merely be the tip of the iceberg'.\nAntonyms\nExpand All\nにほかならない\nにほかならない\nNothing but, None other than, Simply\nN2 Grammar\nにほかならない and にすぎない both express exclusivity but with opposite evaluations. にほかならない emphasizes significance or essential identity, as in それは努力の結果にほかならない (It is nothing but the result of effort). にすぎない downplays importance, as in 僕は一学生にすぎない (I’m just a student).\nRelated\nExpand All\nでしかない\nMerely, Nothing but, No more than\nN2 Grammar\nBoth mean merely or nothing but. にすぎない is neutral and factual, as in 僕は学生にすぎない (I’m just a student). でしかない often carries a negative or limiting nuance, as in 言い訳でしかない (That’s nothing but an excuse).\nVocab Coverage\nAll Bunpro Vocab that appears on this item.\nExpand List\nKnowledge Check\nExamples\n--:--\nSentence\nTranslation\n君\n(\nきみ\n)\nは\n学生\n(\nがくせい\n)\nにすぎない\n。\nYou are\nnothing more than\na student.\n行動\n(\nこうどう\n)\nしなかったら、\n口\n(\nくち\n)\nだけ\nにすぎない\n。\nIf you don't act, then that is\nnothing more than\ntalk.\n運\n(\nうん\n)\nが\n悪\n(\nわる\n)\nい\nだけ\nにすぎない\n。\nIt is\njust\nbad luck. (\nnothing more than\n)\n利害\n(\nりがい\n)\n関係\n(\nかんけい\n)\nがあるから、\n親切\n(\nしんせつ\n)\nにしている\nにすぎない\n。\nSince I have an interest/stake in it, I am\nmerely\nbeing kind. (\nnothing more than\n)\n「いつか\n飲\n(\nの\n)\nみましょう」って\n言\n(\nい\n)\nったけど、あれは\n社交\n(\nしゃこう\n)\n辞令\n(\nじれい\n)\nにすぎない\n。\nI said, 'Let's drink sometime,' but that\nis no more than\nsocial etiquette.\nGet more example sentences!\nPremium users get access to 12 example sentences on all Grammar Points.\nTry Bunpro\nSelf-Study Sentences\nStudy your own way!\nAdd sentences and study them alongside Bunpro sentences.\nTry Bunpro\nOnline\n文型・例文 ～にすぎない\n日本語 NET\nOffline\nThere are no Offline resources listed for 「にすぎない」.\nYou can\nsubmit a resource for review\n. Resources are constantly updated, come back later to see new additions!\nTrack Resources!\nBunpro tracks all of the resources you’ve visited, and offers relevant bookmarks of physical books to help with offline tracking.\nTry Bunpro\nにすぎない – Grammar Discussion\nMost Recent Replies (1 in total)\ndokidokiwakuwaku\nWould だけ or ばかり not be acceptable synonyms for this grammar point? If not, can someone explain the difference in usage? Thank you!\nGot questions about にすぎない?\nJoin us to discuss, ask, and learn together!\nJoin the Discussion\nBunpro\nSimplifying Japanese\nOfficial Apps\nLearn More\nJoin us!\nCompany\nNews\nCareers\nAbout Us\nTestimonials\nAcknowledgements\nFor Teachers\nJapanese\nOfficial Forums\nContent Search\nReading Practice\nGrammar Library\nHiragana & Katakana\nSupport\nContact Us\nSupport & FAQ\n© 2026, Bunpro SRS.\nRead our\nTerms of Service\n,\nPrivacy Policy\nand\nCompany Overview\n.\nMade with\n❤️\nfrom Osaka.\nEnglish",
