      "sourceText": "につれて (JLPT N3) | Bunpro\nLoading user data...\nBunpro\nGrammar Info\nN3 Lesson 8: 5/23\nに\n連\n(\nつ\n)\nれて\nAs…then, In proportion to, (Along) with\nDetails\nExamples\nResources\nにつれて\nAs…then, In proportion to, (Along) with\nDetails\nExamples\nResources\nDetails\nExamples\nResources\nReady to transform your studies?\nLearn N5 in under a month!\nTry now, no credit card required!\nTry Bunpro\nLearn More\nStructure\nVerb［る］\n+\nに\nつれ\n（\nて\n）\nNoun +\nに\nつれ\n（\nて\n）\nDetails\nRegister\nStandard\nAbout につれて\nEnglish\nJapanese\nにつれて\n, or\nに\n連\n(\nつ\n)\nれて\nwhen using kanji, is an expression that may be translated as 'as (A), then (B)', or 'in proportion to (A), (B)'. It is formed through the use of the\ncase marking particle\nに\n, the る - Verb\n連\n(\nつ\n)\nれる 'to take along', and the\nconjunction particle\nて. Literally, the translation is similar to 'being taken along with (A), (B)', or 'in tow with (A), (B)'.\nにつれて\nwill be used after the plain, non-past form of verbs, or nouns.\nAs\n連\n(\nつ\n)\nれる is a transitive verb, (A)\nにつれて\n(B) implies that (A) is causing (B) to happen simultaneously. This does not have to be something that (A) is purposely doing (although it may be), just a 'domino' type effect, where (A) is considered the instigator.\nSynonyms\nExpand All\nにしたがって\nにしたがって\nAs, Following, As then, According to, In accordance with\nN2 Grammar\nBoth express change in tandem and can often be used interchangeably. にしたがって frames it as happening 'in accordance with' another, while につれて emphasizes gradual, proportional change. For example, '話すにしたがって、だんだん打ち解けてきた' and '話すにつれて、だんだん打ち解けてきた' have nearly the same meaning.\nAntonyms\nExpand All\nと\nAnd\nN5 Grammar\nにつれて describes changes that occur in proportion to each other, as one progresses, the other does too. と, on the other hand, is a conditional particle used when one event naturally or habitually leads to another. Unlike につれて, と does not imply a proportional relationship between the events.\nRelated\nExpand All\nに伴って・に伴い\nにともなって\nAs, Due,  Along with, Hand-in-hand with, Resulted in, Be consequent upon\nN2 Grammar\nにつれて and に伴って・に伴い both express one thing happening as a result of or alongside another. につれて emphasizes gradual and proportional change, e.g. '年を取るにつれて体力が落ちる' ('As I age, my stamina declines'). に伴って・に伴い can also be used with one-time or habitual events, e.g. '津波は地震に伴い発生する' ('Tsunamis occur together with earthquakes').\nともなると・にもなると\nとなると\nWhen, If, Once, As\nN1 Grammar\nBoth につれて and ともなると・にもなると describe changes that arise with conditions, but differ in nuance. につれて describes gradual, parallel change over time, e.g. '年を取るにつれて体力が落ちる' ('As I age, my stamina declines'). ともなると・にもなると marks a turning point or elevated situation, e.g. '社長ともなると責任が重い' ('Once you become a company president, the responsibility is heavy').\nと共に\nとともに\nTogether with, At the same time,  As well as\nN3 Grammar\nと共に and につれて are similar in that both can be translated as 'together with', but differ in nuance. と共に can express simultaneous actions or states, or the idea of accompaniment, e.g. '厳しいと共に優しい' ('kind as well as strict'). につれて highlights proportional change over time, e.g. '年を取るにつれて体力が落ちる' ('As I get older, my stamina declines').\nVocab Coverage\nAll Bunpro Vocab that appears on this item.\nExpand List\nKnowledge Check\nExamples\n--:--\nSentence\nTranslation\n日\n(\nひ\n)\nがたつ\nに\n連\n(\nつ\n)\nれて\n、\n怪我\n(\nけが\n)\nが\n悪化\n(\nあっか\n)\nしてきた。\nAs\nthe days go by, my injury gets worse and worse.\nこちらの\n木\n(\nき\n)\nが\n大\n(\nおお\n)\nきくなる\nに\n連\n(\nつ\n)\nれて\n、\n影\n(\nかげ\n)\nが\n広\n(\nひろ\n)\nがる。\nAs\nthese trees grow tall, their shade spreads.\n子供\n(\nこども\n)\nは、\n成長\n(\nせいちょう\n)\nする\nに\n連\n(\nつ\n)\nれて\n、\n性格\n(\nせいかく\n)\nが\n変\n(\nか\n)\nわる。\nAlong with\ntheir growth, the personality of children changes.\n進\n(\nすす\n)\nむ\nに\n連\n(\nつ\n)\nれて\n道\n(\nみち\n)\nがどんどん\n狭\n(\nせま\n)\nくなるから\n心配\n(\nしんぱい\n)\nになってきた。\nAs\nI continued on, the road grew increasingly more narrow, so I started to feel anxious.\n経済\n(\nけいざい\n)\nの\n発展\n(\nはってん\n)\nに\n連\n(\nつ\n)\nれて\n一般\n(\nいっぱん\n)\n市民\n(\nしみん\n)\nの\n日常\n(\nにちじょう\n)\n生活\n(\nせいかつ\n)\nは\n良\n(\nよ\n)\nくなっていく。\nAs\nthe economy develops, the daily life of citizens improves.\nGet more example sentences!\nPremium users get access to 12 example sentences on all Grammar Points.\nTry Bunpro\nSelf-Study Sentences\nStudy your own way!\nAdd sentences and study them alongside Bunpro sentences.\nTry Bunpro\nOnline\n〜につれて VS 〜に伴って\n日本語の森\nにつれ / につれて\nJapaneseTest4You\n文型・例文 - ～につれて\n日本語 NET\nOffline\nTobira\nPage 308\nTrack Resources!\nBunpro tracks all of the resources you’ve visited, and offers relevant bookmarks of physical books to help with offline tracking.\nTry Bunpro\nにつれて – Grammar Discussion\nThere's currently no discussion for につれて\nAsk questions and learn together with other Bunpro users!\nJoin the Discussion\nBunpro\nSimplifying Japanese\nOfficial Apps\nLearn More\nJoin us!\nCompany\nNews\nCareers\nAbout Us\nTestimonials\nAcknowledgements\nFor Teachers\nJapanese\nOfficial Forums\nContent Search\nReading Practice\nGrammar Library\nHiragana & Katakana\nSupport\nContact Us\nSupport & FAQ\n© 2026, Bunpro SRS.\nRead our\nTerms of Service\n,\nPrivacy Policy\nand\nCompany Overview\n.\nMade with\n❤️\nfrom Osaka.\nEnglish",
