      "sourceText": "に伴って・に伴い (JLPT N2) | Bunpro\nLoading user data...\nBunpro\nGrammar Info\nN2 Lesson 2: 18/24\nに\n伴\n(\nともな\n)\nって\nAs, Due,  Along with, Hand-in-hand with, Resulted in, Be consequent upon\nDetails\nExamples\nResources\nに伴って・に伴い\nAs, Due,  Along with, Hand-in-hand with, Resulted in, Be consequent upon\nDetails\nExamples\nResources\nDetails\nExamples\nResources\nReady to transform your studies?\nLearn N5 in under a month!\nTry now, no credit card required!\nTry Bunpro\nLearn More\nStructure\nVerb［る］\n+（\nの\n）+\nに\n伴\n(\nともな\n)\nっ\nて\n(1)\nVerb［る］\n+（\nの\n）+\nに\n伴\n(\nともな\n)\nう\n+ Noun\nNoun +\nに\n伴\n(\nともな\n)\nっ\nて\n(1)\nNoun +\nに\n伴\n(\nともな\n)\nう\n+ Noun\n(1)\nに\n伴\n(\nともな\n)\nい\nDetails\nRegister\nStandard\nAbout に伴って・に伴い\nEnglish\nJapanese\nWhen the う-Verb\n伴\n(\nともな\n)\nう 'to accompany' in its て-form is used with に and attached to the end of nouns or verbs in their dictionary forms, it is regularly translated as 'due to (A), (B)', 'hand in hand with (A), (B)', or 'along with (A), (B)'. In all of these meanings, the base interpretation of 'to accompany' is being highlighted.\nAs 'accompanying' does not specifically indicate that (A) is controlling (B), this grammar structure may be used simply to indicate things that happen at the same time, rather than when something is being directly caused by the first. However, (A) having a strong influence on the change of (B) is usually implied.\nに\n伴\n(\nともな\n)\nう\nmay also appear directly before another noun when it is being modified by the verb.\nに\n伴\n(\nともな\n)\nって\nis used both for events that are progressively changing at the same time, and momentary events that cause a sudden change.\nSynonyms\nExpand All\nにしたがって\nにしたがって\nAs, Following, As then, According to, In accordance with\nN2 Grammar\nに伴って・に伴い describes changes in one thing due to another, in a proportional or cause-and-effect manner, as in 人口減少に伴って (along with the declining population). にしたがって can overlap in this usage, but it also extends to a broader sense of following rules or standards, as in 指示に従って (according to instructions).\nと共に\nとともに\nTogether with, At the same time,  As well as\nN3 Grammar\nに伴って・に伴い and と共に both express things happening in connection with another event. と共に emphasizes simultaneity or shared experience, e.g. '成長と共に責任も増える' ('Responsibility grows along with maturity'). に伴って・に伴い emphasizes causality or consequential change, often in formal contexts, e.g. '経済の発展に伴って生活水準が向上した' ('As the economy developed, living standards improved').\nRelated\nExpand All\nに沿って\nにそって\nAlong, In accordance with, In line with\nN2 Grammar\nに沿って and に伴って・に伴い both imply corresponding relationships, but with different nuances. に沿って means in line with in literal or figurative contexts, as in 点線に沿って (along the dotted line) or スケジュールに沿って (in line with the schedule). に伴って・に伴い suggests one change occurring along with another, as in 人口減少に伴って (along with the declining population).\nにつれて\nにつれて\nAs…then, In proportion to, (Along) with\nN3 Grammar\nにつれて and に伴って・に伴い both express one thing happening as a result of or alongside another. につれて emphasizes gradual and proportional change, e.g. '年を取るにつれて体力が落ちる' ('As I age, my stamina declines'). に伴って・に伴い can also be used with one-time or habitual events, e.g. '津波は地震に伴い発生する' ('Tsunamis occur together with earthquakes').\nきっかけ\nきっかけ\nLead to, Because of, As a start or trigger of, An opportunity\nN2 Grammar\nBoth can describe one event influencing another, but with very different nuance. きっかけ refers to something that triggered or led to a change, as in 入院をきっかけにタバコをやめた (I gave up smoking on the occasion of my hospitalization). に伴って・に伴い is more formal, often expressing a broader causal relationship, as in 高齢化に伴い人口が激減した (The population rapidly declined along with the aging of the population).\nを契機に\nをけいきに\nLead to, As a good opportunity to, As a result of, As a trigger\nN2 Grammar\nBoth are formal expressions describing one event influencing another, but differ slightly in usage. を契機に emphasizes a turning point or opportunity that led to change, as in 入院を契機にタバコをやめた (I gave up smoking on the occasion of my hospitalization). に伴って・に伴い often appears in news reports to describe cause-and-effect relationships.\nと並んで\nとならんで\nIn line with, Comparable with, Along with, Just like, As … as\nN3 Grammar\nBoth に伴って and と並んで connect two elements, but differ in meaning. に伴って expresses a causal or accompanying relationship where one thing changes in response to another, e.g. '経済の成長に伴って、生活水準も上がった' ('As the economy grew, the standard of living also rose'). と並んで indicates comparable qualities without implying cause, e.g. 'ドラえもんと並んで人気のアニメ' ('an anime as popular as Doraemon').\nVocab Coverage\nAll Bunpro Vocab that appears on this item.\nExpand List\nKnowledge Check\nExamples\n--:--\nSentence\nTranslation\n春\n(\nはる\n)\nが\n始\n(\nはじ\n)\nまる\nに\n伴\n(\nともな\n)\nって\n、\n植生\n(\nしょくせい\n)\nは\n復活\n(\nふっかつ\n)\nする。\nWith\nthe beginning of spring, the vegetation returns. (\nalong with・consequent upon\n)\n医学\n(\nいがく\n)\nの\n進歩\n(\nしんぽ\n)\nに\n伴\n(\nともな\n)\nって\n平均\n(\nへいきん\n)\n寿命\n(\nじゅみょう\n)\nが\n伸\n(\nの\n)\nびています。\nAlong with\nthe advancement of medical sciences, the average life expectancy is increasing.\n円\n(\nえん\n)\n高\n(\nだか\n)\nに\n伴\n(\nともな\n)\nい\n輸出\n(\nゆしゅつ\n)\nの\n量\n(\nりょう\n)\nは\n減\n(\nへ\n)\nる。\nAs\nthe value of the yen rises, the volume of export decreases. (\nalong with・consequent upon\n)\n火傷\n(\nやけど\n)\nに\n伴\n(\nともな\n)\nう\n痛\n(\nいた\n)\nみは\n神経\n(\nしんけい\n)\nへの\n刺激\n(\nしげき\n)\nが\n原因\n(\nげんいん\n)\nだとされている。\nPain\nassociated with\nburns is considered to be caused by nerve stimulation.\n城\n(\nしろ\n)\nの\n改修\n(\nかいしゅう\n)\n中\n(\nちゅう\n)\n、\n床\n(\nゆか\n)\nの\n修理\n(\nしゅうり\n)\nに\n伴\n(\nともな\n)\nって\n、\n壁\n(\nかべ\n)\nも\n塗\n(\nぬ\n)\nりなおされた。\nDuring the castle renovation,\nalong with\nthe floor repairs, the walls were also repainted.\nGet more example sentences!\nPremium users get access to 12 example sentences on all Grammar Points.\nTry Bunpro\nSelf-Study Sentences\nStudy your own way!\nAdd sentences and study them alongside Bunpro sentences.\nTry Bunpro\nOnline\nFurther Examples\nJapaneseTest4You\nOffline\n新完全マスター文法、N2\nPage 42-2\nTrack Resources!\nBunpro tracks all of the resources you’ve visited, and offers relevant bookmarks of physical books to help with offline tracking.\nTry Bunpro\nに伴って・に伴い – Grammar Discussion\nMost Recent Replies (4 in total)\nFuga\nHey @ArsDiaboli !\nWe apologize for the late response.\nに伴って・に伴い・に伴う is usually used to express ‘As A changes, B also changes’, but it can also be used to express ‘A happens at the same time as B’.\nFor example, 火傷に伴う痛みは神経への刺激が原因だとされている。Here, に伴う is used as ‘associated with’ because this sentence is describing how ‘a burn is painful because there is nerve stimulation going on at the same time.’\nWe hope that answers your question!\nJoellaumelb\nHi @Fuga\nHope you are well.\nCould you please clarify why this phrase uses a negative form of \"に伴って”？\n円高にともない輸出の量は減る。\nAs the value of the yen rises, the volume of export decreases.\n[along with・consequent upon]\nThanks!\nFuga\nHey @Joellaumelb !\nに伴い is not the negative form of 伴って, but it is the conjunctive form of 伴う. 伴って is 伴い conjugated using the て-form.\nIn most cases they can be used interchangeably.\nHope that clears it up!\nGot questions about に伴って・に伴い?\nJoin us to discuss, ask, and learn together!\nJoin the Discussion\nBunpro\nSimplifying Japanese\nOfficial Apps\nLearn More\nJoin us!\nCompany\nNews\nCareers\nAbout Us\nTestimonials\nAcknowledgements\nFor Teachers\nJapanese\nOfficial Forums\nContent Search\nReading Practice\nGrammar Library\nHiragana & Katakana\nSupport\nContact Us\nSupport & FAQ\n© 2026, Bunpro SRS.\nRead our\nTerms of Service\n,\nPrivacy Policy\nand\nCompany Overview\n.\nMade with\n❤️\nfrom Osaka.\nEnglish",
