      "sourceText": "一方で (JLPT N3) | Bunpro\nLoading user data...\nBunpro\nGrammar Info\nN3 Lesson 8: 16/23\n一方\n(\nいっぽう\n)\nで\nOn the other hand, At the same time, While\nDetails\nExamples\nResources\n一方で\nOn the other hand, At the same time, While\nDetails\nExamples\nResources\nDetails\nExamples\nResources\nReady to transform your studies?\nLearn N5 in under a month!\nTry now, no credit card required!\nTry Bunpro\nLearn More\nStructure\nVerb +\n一方\n(\nいっぽう\n)\n（\nで\n）\n［い］Adjective\n+\n一方\n(\nいっぽう\n)\n（\nで\n）\n［な］Adjective +\nな\n(1)\n+\n一方\n(\nいっぽう\n)\n（\nで\n）\nNoun +\nの\n(1)\n+\n一方\n(\nいっぽう\n)\n（\nで\n）\nPhrase。\n一方\n(\nいっぽう\n)\n(2)\n+ Phrase\n(1)\nで\nある\n(2)\nその\n一方\n(\nいっぽう\n)\n(\nで\n)\nDetails\nRegister\nStandard\nAbout 一方で\nEnglish\nJapanese\n一方\n(\nいっぽう\n)\nで\nis a combination of the\nnoun\n一方\n(\nいっぽう\n)\n'one direction', and the\ncase marking particle\nで, in its nuance as 'at'. Together, they are used in a similar way to a\nconjunction particle\n, carrying the meaning of 'on the other hand', 'at the same time', or 'while'.\n一方\n(\nいっぽう\n)\nで\nmay be used after the\nattributive form\nof other words, or at the beginning of new phrases.\nAs\n一方\n(\nいっぽう\n)\nで\nhas a literal meaning similar to 'at the (A) side', or 'in the (A) direction', it is expressing that another direction also exists, which may then be compared or contrasted with (A).\nCaution\nDo not confuse\n一方\n(\nいっぽう\n)\nで\n, with\n一方\n(\nいっぽう\n)\nだ\n(or で in its conjunctive form). The expression that uses the で particle means 'at one direction/side', while the expression that utilizes the\nauxiliary verb\nだ (or で in its conjunctive form) means 'in one direction'.\nThe overall context of the sentence will usually reveal whether the conjunctive form of だ (で) is being used, or the actual で particle.\nRelated\nExpand All\n一方だ\nいっぽうだ\nMore and more, Continue to, Keep on, -er and -er\nN3 Grammar\nWhile they look similar, 一方で and 一方だ serve different functions. 一方で shows contrast between two ideas or situations, e.g. '一方で反対する人もいる' ('On the other hand, some people are against it'). 一方だ follows verbs to describe trends, e.g. '物価は上がる一方だ' ('Prices keep rising').\n反面\nはんめん\nWhile, On the other hand, Although, However, On the flip side\nN2 Grammar\n一方で and 反面 both show contrast, but differ in tone. 一方で is neutral and presents parallel or opposing facts, e.g. '一方で経済は成長している' ('On the other hand, the economy is growing'). 反面 highlights a downside or contradiction, e.g. '便利な反面、依存しやすい' ('While convenient, it's also easy to become dependent').\nかたわら\nかたわら\nWhile, Besides, In addition to\nN1 Grammar\nかたわら and 一方で both describe two actions or conditions, but differ in nuance. かたわら implies doing something secondary alongside a main activity, e.g. '彼は本業のかたわら小説を書いている' ('He writes novels alongside his main job'). 一方で marks contrast or coexistence between broader situations, e.g. '一方で都市化が進んでいる' ('Meanwhile, urbanization is advancing').\nVocab Coverage\nAll Bunpro Vocab that appears on this item.\nExpand List\nKnowledge Check\nExamples\n--:--\nSentence\nTranslation\nこの\n靴\n(\nくつ\n)\nは、\n温\n(\nあたた\n)\nかい\n一方\n(\nいっぽう\n)\nで\n、\n重\n(\nおも\n)\nいです。\nThese shoes are warm but\non the other hand\nthey are heavy.\nあの\n食\n(\nた\n)\nべ\n物\n(\nもの\n)\nは\n体\n(\nからだ\n)\nに\n良\n(\nい\n)\nい\n一方\n(\nいっぽう\n)\nで\n、\n食\n(\nた\n)\nべ\n過\n(\nす\n)\nぎたら、\n体\n(\nからだ\n)\nに\n悪\n(\nわる\n)\nい。\nOn the one hand\n, that food is good for your body.\nOn the other hand\n, if you eat too much, it is bad for you.\n彼\n(\nかれ\n)\nの\n会社\n(\nかいしゃ\n)\nが\n儲\n(\nもう\n)\nかる\n一方\n(\nいっぽう\n)\nで\n、うちの\n会社\n(\nかいしゃ\n)\nは\n経営\n(\nけいえい\n)\n状態\n(\nじょうたい\n)\nが\n悪化\n(\nあっか\n)\nしている。\nHis company seems to be profitable, but,\non the other hand\n, the condition of our administration is growing worse.\n友人\n(\nゆうじん\n)\nたちがスキーを\n楽\n(\nたの\n)\nしむ\n一方\n(\nいっぽう\n)\nで\n、\n私\n(\nわたし\n)\nは\n働\n(\nはたら\n)\nかなくてはいけない。\nMy friends are having a fun time skiing, but I,\non the other hand\n, have to work.\n会社\n(\nかいしゃ\n)\nではいい\n上司\n(\nじょうし\n)\nだが、その\n一方\n(\nいっぽう\n)\nで\n、\n家\n(\nいえ\n)\nでは\n酒乱\n(\nしゅらん\n)\nだ。\nHe is a good boss at the company, but,\nat the same time\n, he is a violent drunk at home.\nGet more example sentences!\nPremium users get access to 12 example sentences on all Grammar Points.\nTry Bunpro\nSelf-Study Sentences\nStudy your own way!\nAdd sentences and study them alongside Bunpro sentences.\nTry Bunpro\nOnline\nN3 Pattern: Difference of 「～かわりに」、「～反面」、「～一方（で）」\nJStackExchange\n一方では\nE-Japanese\nOffline\n[AIAIJ] An Integrated Approach to Intermediate Japanese\nPage 248\nTobira\nPage 215\nTrack Resources!\nBunpro tracks all of the resources you’ve visited, and offers relevant bookmarks of physical books to help with offline tracking.\nTry Bunpro\n一方で – Grammar Discussion\nThere's currently no discussion for 一方で\nAsk questions and learn together with other Bunpro users!\nJoin the Discussion\nBunpro\nSimplifying Japanese\nOfficial Apps\nLearn More\nJoin us!\nCompany\nNews\nCareers\nAbout Us\nTestimonials\nAcknowledgements\nFor Teachers\nJapanese\nOfficial Forums\nContent Search\nReading Practice\nGrammar Library\nHiragana & Katakana\nSupport\nContact Us\nSupport & FAQ\n© 2026, Bunpro SRS.\nRead our\nTerms of Service\n,\nPrivacy Policy\nand\nCompany Overview\n.\nMade with\n❤️\nfrom Osaka.\nEnglish",
