      "sourceText": "一方だ (JLPT N3) | Bunpro\nLoading user data...\nBunpro\nGrammar Info\nN3 Lesson 8: 15/23\n一方\n(\nいっぽう\n)\nだ\nMore and more, Continue to, Keep on, -er and -er\nThe verb must express change (e.g. 増える、下がる、or verbs ending with …なる、…てくる、…ていく etc.)\nDetails\nExamples\nResources\n一方だ\nMore and more, Continue to, Keep on, -er and -er\nDetails\nExamples\nResources\nDetails\nExamples\nResources\nReady to transform your studies?\nLearn N5 in under a month!\nTry now, no credit card required!\nTry Bunpro\nLearn More\nStructure\nStandard\nPolite\nVerb +\n一方\n(\nいっぽう\n)\nだ\nVerb +\n一方\n(\nいっぽう\n)\nで\n+  Phrase\nDetails\nRegister\nFormal\nAbout 一方だ\nEnglish\nJapanese\n一方\n(\nいっぽう\n)\nis a\nnoun\nthat is often seen after verbs, in order to convey the meaning of 'more and more (A)', 'continuing to (A)', or 'getting (A)er and (A)er'.\n一方\n(\nいっぽう\n)\nwill be paired with the\nauxiliary verb\nだ\n(at the end of sentences), or で, だ's\nconjunctive form\nwhen it will be followed by some sort of explanation.\nAs the literal meaning of\n一方\n(\nいっぽう\n)\nis 'single direction', it may be used with things that are increasing, decreasing, intensifying, or weakening, so long as the shift is all in a single direction.\nCaution\n一方\n(\nいっぽう\n)\nmay only be used with verbs that express some kind of change, as\n一方\n(\nいっぽう\n)\nitself does not express change, just a continuing direction.\nRelated\nExpand All\n一方で\nいっぽうで\nOn the other hand, At the same time, While\nN3 Grammar\nWhile they look similar, 一方で and 一方だ serve different functions. 一方で shows contrast between two ideas or situations, e.g. '一方で反対する人もいる' ('On the other hand, some people are against it'). 一方だ follows verbs to describe trends, e.g. '物価は上がる一方だ' ('Prices keep rising').\nつづける\nつづける\nTo continue\nN4 Grammar\nつづける and 一方だ both indicate continuation but differ in tone. つづける means a simple ongoing action, e.g. 減り続けている 'is still decreasing'. 一方だ follows dictionary-form verbs and adds a sense of progression in one direction, often negatively, e.g., 減る一方だ 'is getting worse and worse'.\nますます\nますます\nIncreasingly, More and more, Decreasingly, Less and less, Keep -ing\nN3 Grammar\nBoth 一方だ and ますます express progressive change, but differ in usage. 一方だ follows verbs, often in formal or objective contexts to describe trends, e.g. '物価は上がる一方だ' ('Prices keep rising'). ますます has a similar nuance, but precedes the phrase or sentence, e.g. '彼の人気はますます高まっている' ('His popularity is increasing more and more').\nどんどん\nProgressively, Rapidly increasing, More and more\nN4 Grammar\nどんどん is an adverb that implies rapid or dramatic change, often in leaps and bounds, and is common in everyday speech. In contrast, 一方だ is more formal and used to describe ongoing change that continues beyond the speaker's control. Structurally, 一方だ follows the verb, unlike どんどん, which appears before it.\nいよいよ\nいよいよ\nAt last, Finally, More and more\nN2 Grammar\nBoth 一方だ and いよいよ express change, but differ in usage. 一方だ follows verbs, often in formal or objective contexts to describe trends, e.g. '物価は上がる一方だ' ('Prices keep rising'). いよいよ suggests something is finally or imminently happening, often with anticipation, e.g. 'いよいよ試合が始まる' ('The match is about to begin').\nば〜ほど\nば～ほど\nThe more…the more\nN3 Grammar\nBoth can be used to describe change, but with different patterns. ば〜ほど expresses a proportional relationship between two things, like 'the more (A), the more (B)', e.g. 練習すればするほど上手になる ('The more you practice, the better you get.') 一方だ shows a continuous, one-way change in a single direction, e.g. 物価は上がる一方だ ('Prices just keep rising.')\nばかりだ\n(Only) continue to, Keep on -ing, More and more\nN3 Grammar\nばかりだ and 一方だ are similar in that both express continuous or progressive change. However, ばかりだ is typically used with negative developments and often carries a more subjective tone, e.g. 状況は悪くなるばかりだ ('The situation keeps getting worse'). 一方だ, on the other hand, sounds more neutral or objective, and doesn't necessarily imply a negative trend, e.g. 人口は増える一方だ ('The population keeps increasing').\nVocab Coverage\nAll Bunpro Vocab that appears on this item.\nExpand List\nKnowledge Check\nExamples\n--:--\nSentence\nTranslation\n災害\n(\nさいがい\n)\nは\n増\n(\nふ\n)\nえる\n一方\n(\nいっぽう\n)\nです\n。\nMore and more\ndisasters happen.\n会社\n(\nかいしゃ\n)\nの\n財政\n(\nざいせい\n)\nは\n厳\n(\nきび\n)\nしくなる\n一方\n(\nいっぽう\n)\nだ\n。\nThe financial situation of the company\ncontinues to\nget\nmore and more\nstrict.\nうちの\n町\n(\nまち\n)\nの\n人口\n(\nじんこう\n)\nは\n減\n(\nへ\n)\nる\n一方\n(\nいっぽう\n)\nだ\n。\nThe population of my town\nkeeps on\ndecreasing.\nこのままだと\n借金\n(\nしゃっきん\n)\nが\n増\n(\nふ\n)\nえる\n一方\n(\nいっぽう\n)\nだ\n。\nIf I keep going on like this, my debts will\ncontinue to\nincrease.\n残念\n(\nざんねん\n)\nながらこんな\n事件\n(\nじけん\n)\nが\n増\n(\nふ\n)\nえる\n一方\n(\nいっぽう\n)\nだ。\nUnfortunately, there are\nmore and more\ncases like these.\nGet more example sentences!\nPremium users get access to 12 example sentences on all Grammar Points.\nTry Bunpro\nSelf-Study Sentences\nStudy your own way!\nAdd sentences and study them alongside Bunpro sentences.\nTry Bunpro\nOnline\n一方だ\n日本語教師のN1et\nOffline\nThere are no Offline resources listed for 「一方だ」.\nYou can\nsubmit a resource for review\n. Resources are constantly updated, come back later to see new additions!\nTrack Resources!\nBunpro tracks all of the resources you’ve visited, and offers relevant bookmarks of physical books to help with offline tracking.\nTry Bunpro\n一方だ – Grammar Discussion\nMost Recent Replies (5 in total)\nlantana\nThanks for your answer. Unfortunately I am just getting them marked wrong instead of the “Could you say it another way?” notification.\nmrnoone\nHey\nWe have fixed it, so ばかり should be working from now on\nThanks a lot for pointing this error, and sorry for causing the inconvenience\njeleni-skraje\nGot questions about 一方だ?\nJoin us to discuss, ask, and learn together!\nJoin the Discussion\nBunpro\nSimplifying Japanese\nOfficial Apps\nLearn More\nJoin us!\nCompany\nNews\nCareers\nAbout Us\nTestimonials\nAcknowledgements\nFor Teachers\nJapanese\nOfficial Forums\nContent Search\nReading Practice\nGrammar Library\nHiragana & Katakana\nSupport\nContact Us\nSupport & FAQ\n© 2026, Bunpro SRS.\nRead our\nTerms of Service\n,\nPrivacy Policy\nand\nCompany Overview\n.\nMade with\n❤️\nfrom Osaka.\nEnglish",
