      "sourceText": "反面 (JLPT N2) | Bunpro\nLoading user data...\nBunpro\nGrammar Info\nN2 Lesson 6: 3/20\n反面\n(\nはんめん\n)\nWhile, On the other hand, Although, However, On the flip side\nDetails\nExamples\nResources\n反面\nWhile, On the other hand, Although, However, On the flip side\nDetails\nExamples\nResources\nDetails\nExamples\nResources\nReady to transform your studies?\nLearn N5 in under a month!\nTry now, no credit card required!\nTry Bunpro\nLearn More\nStructure\nVerb +\n反面\n(\nはんめん\n)\n［い］Adjective\n+\n反面\n(\nはんめん\n)\n［な］Adjective\n+\nな\n(1)\n+\n反面\n(\nはんめん\n)\nNoun +\nである\n+\n反面\n(\nはんめん\n)\nPhrase +\nが\n+ （、）+\n反面\n(\nはんめん\n)\n(1)\nである\nDetails\nRegister\nStandard\nAbout 反面\nEnglish\nJapanese\n反面\n(\nはんめん\n)\n, a noun meaning 'the opposing side', is a construction in Japanese that appears between two phrases, to show two contrasting or opposite features of a single person or thing. This usually translates as 'while (A), (B)', 'although (A), also (B)', 'on the other hand to (A), (B)'.\nBeing a noun,\n反面\n(\nはんめん\n)\n, can be used after any word that could create a modified noun, such as verbs, い-Adjectives, な-Adjectives, or even other nouns followed by である.\nCaution\nBecause\n反面\n(\nはんめん\n)\nshows contrast between conflicting sides of something, it will most often describe a positive and a negative, but cannot describe a positive and another positive, or a negative and another negative.\nRelated\nExpand All\n一方で\nいっぽうで\nOn the other hand, At the same time, While\nN3 Grammar\n一方で and 反面 both show contrast, but differ in tone. 一方で is neutral and presents parallel or opposing facts, e.g. '一方で経済は成長している' ('On the other hand, the economy is growing'). 反面 highlights a downside or contradiction, e.g. '便利な反面、依存しやすい' ('While convenient, it's also easy to become dependent').\nに対して\nにたいして\nIn contrast to, While, In regard to, Whereas\nN3 Grammar\nBoth express contrast, but their nuance differs. に対して typically compares two things with opposing qualities, e.g. 田中先生が厳しいのに対して、鈴木先生は優しい ('Whereas Prof. Tanaka is strict, Prof. Suzuki is lenient'). 反面 focuses on two sides of the same situation, e.g. 都会の生活は便利な反面、お金がかかる ('Life in the big city is convenient, but expensive'). に対して also has a 'toward (A)' usage, which 反面 does not.\nVocab Coverage\nAll Bunpro Vocab that appears on this item.\nExpand List\nKnowledge Check\nExamples\n--:--\nSentence\nTranslation\n商品\n(\nしょうひん\n)\nが\n豪華\n(\nごうか\n)\nである\n反面\n(\nはんめん\n)\n、\n参加\n(\nさんか\n)\n費\n(\nひ\n)\nが\n高額\n(\nこうがく\n)\nだ。\nWhile\nthe products may be luxurious, the participation fee is high.\n彼\n(\nかれ\n)\nは\n慎重\n(\nしんちょう\n)\nな\n反面\n(\nはんめん\n)\n、\n消極\n(\nしょうきょく\n)\n的\n(\nてき\n)\nなところがあります。\nHe is cautious, but on\nthe other hand\n, he also has a passive side.\n一人暮\n(\nひとりぐ\n)\nらしは\n楽\n(\nたの\n)\nしい\n反面\n(\nはんめん\n)\n、\n自分\n(\nじぶん\n)\nで\n料理\n(\nりょうり\n)\nしたり\n掃除\n(\nそうじ\n)\nしたりする\n必要\n(\nひつよう\n)\nもある。\nWhile\nliving alone is fun, it is also necessary for you to do all the cooking, cleaning, and the like.\n厳\n(\nきび\n)\nしいトレーニングを\n積\n(\nつ\n)\nむと\n筋力\n(\nきんりょく\n)\nはつく\n反面\n(\nはんめん\n)\n、\n風邪\n(\nかぜ\n)\nをひきやすくなるらしい。\nRelentlessly training builds physical strength,\non the other hand\n, I seem to become more susceptible to catching a cold.\n消防署\n(\nしょうぼうしょ\n)\nが\n近\n(\nちか\n)\nくにあると\n安心\n(\nあんしん\n)\nできる\n反面\n(\nはんめん\n)\n、\n夜中\n(\nやちゅう\n)\nにサイレンがなるから\n大変\n(\nたいへん\n)\nだ。\nBeing close to the fire station gives a sense of safety,\non the other hand\n, since sirens go off in the middle of the night, it can be troublesome.\nGet more example sentences!\nPremium users get access to 12 example sentences on all Grammar Points.\nTry Bunpro\nSelf-Study Sentences\nStudy your own way!\nAdd sentences and study them alongside Bunpro sentences.\nTry Bunpro\nOnline\nAdditional breakdown and sentences\nJapaneseTest4You\nDifferences between かわりに, 反面, and 一方で\nJapanese StackExchange\n接続・意味・使い方・例文\nにほんごの里\nOffline\n新完全マスター N3\nPage 24-2\nTrack Resources!\nBunpro tracks all of the resources you’ve visited, and offers relevant bookmarks of physical books to help with offline tracking.\nTry Bunpro\n反面 – Grammar Discussion\nThere's currently no discussion for 反面\nAsk questions and learn together with other Bunpro users!\nJoin the Discussion\nBunpro\nSimplifying Japanese\nOfficial Apps\nLearn More\nJoin us!\nCompany\nNews\nCareers\nAbout Us\nTestimonials\nAcknowledgements\nFor Teachers\nJapanese\nOfficial Forums\nContent Search\nReading Practice\nGrammar Library\nHiragana & Katakana\nSupport\nContact Us\nSupport & FAQ\n© 2026, Bunpro SRS.\nRead our\nTerms of Service\n,\nPrivacy Policy\nand\nCompany Overview\n.\nMade with\n❤️\nfrom Osaka.\nEnglish",
