      "sourceText": "であれ (JLPT N1) | Bunpro\nLoading user data...\nBunpro\nGrammar Info\nN1 Lesson 2: 13/18\nであれ\nEven if, Even, No matter\nDetails\nExamples\nResources\nであれ\nEven if, Even, No matter\nDetails\nExamples\nResources\nDetails\nExamples\nResources\nReady to transform your studies?\nLearn N5 in under a month!\nTry now, no credit card required!\nTry Bunpro\nLearn More\nStructure\nNoun +\nであれ\n［な］Adjective\n+\nであれ\nWH-Word +\nであれ\nDetails\nRegister\nFormal\nAbout であれ\nEnglish\nJapanese\nFunctioning as an extension of\nである\n, the formal copula that is a combination of the\nconjunctive form\nof the\nauxiliary verb\nだ, and the う-Verb ある,\nであれ\nor\nであろうと\nwill be used in order to express strong will or conviction.\nあれ is simply the\nimperative form\nof ある, while あろうと is the positive volitional form combined with the case-marking particle と. Both structures are usually translated as 'even if (A), (B)', or 'no matter if (A), (B)'. Despite this, the more literal meaning of each is closer to 'so it's (A), (B) still won't be affected'. This just emphasizes the fact that (A) is of no relation to the result, like saying 'so what if it is' in English.\nBoth\nであれ\nand\nであろうと\nwill primarily attach to nouns in sentences that express some kind of question or assumption through words like どんな or たとえ.\nAs both\nであれ\nand\nであろうと\nuse structures that indicate strong will, these grammar patterns will frequently be used in sentences where the speaker is expressing their opinions or resolutions.\nSynonyms\nExpand All\nにせよ・にしろ\nにせよ\nEven if, Even though, No matter, Whether… or\nN2 Grammar\nBoth can mean even if or no matter, but nuance differs. にせよ・にしろ stresses the speaker’s strong insistence, as in 学生にせよ社会人にせよ責任はある (Even if you’re a student or a worker, you have responsibility). であれ is more formal and written, as in 理由が何であれ許されない (No matter what the reason, it’s unforgivable).\nにしろ～にしろ\nにしろ〜にしろ\nWhether… or\nN2 Grammar\nにしろ～にしろ can follow verbs and broader phrases, as in 勉強するにしろ遊ぶにしろ全力でやれ (Whether you study or play, do it wholeheartedly). であれ follows nouns, な-adjectives, or wh-words and is more formal, as in どんな結果であれ受け入れるしかない (Whatever the result, we must accept it).\nRelated\nExpand All\nであれ〜であれ\nWhether or, Or, No matter which, In either case\nN1 Grammar\nThese are essentially the same grammar point, expressing no matter if one thing is true, the result does not change. The difference is that であれ～であれ is specifically used when comparing multiple options, e.g. 子どもであれ大人であれ 'no matter if they're a child or adult', while であれ is used with single examples, e.g. 大人であれ 'even if they're an adult' or with question expressions, e.g. 誰であれ 'no matter who it is'.\n何しろ\nなにしろ\nNo wonder, After all, In fact, Because, At any rate\nN2 Grammar\n何しろ appears at the start of a sentence to give a reason, like after all, as in 何しろ忙しいので行けません (After all, I’m busy, so I can’t go). であれ follows nouns, な-adjectives, or wh-words to mean even if or no matter, often in formal contexts, as in 理由が何であれ許されない (No matter what the reason, it’s unforgivable).\nとはいえ\nとはいえ\nThough, Although (I admit that), Be that as it may, Nonetheless\nN1 Grammar\nとはいえ and であれ are similar in that they both express a sort of contrast, but とはいえ 'although (one could say)' specifically qualifies a statement by saying one thing might be true, but there is more to the matter, e.g. 日本人とはいえ、フランスで生まれ育った ('Though she may be Japanese, she was born and raised in France.'). Though they can overlap in some cases, であれ 'even'/'no matter' is often used together with question words, e.g. 理由は何であれ 'no matter the reason', while とはいえ cannot be used this way.\nVocab Coverage\nAll Bunpro Vocab that appears on this item.\nExpand List\nKnowledge Check\nExamples\n--:--\nSentence\nTranslation\n誰\n(\nだれ\n)\nであれ\n全\n(\nすべ\n)\nての\n人々\n(\nひとびと\n)\nは\n同様\n(\nどうよう\n)\nに\n死\n(\nし\n)\nぬ。\nNo matter\nwho you are, all people die similarly.\n小説\n(\nしょうせつ\n)\n：「どのような\n状況\n(\nじょうきょう\n)\nであれ\n、\n逃\n(\nに\n)\nげることは\n許\n(\nゆる\n)\nされない。」\nNovel\n: '\nNo matter\nthe circumstances, running away is unforgivable.'\n何\n(\nなん\n)\nであれ\n、\n両親\n(\nりょうしん\n)\nにとっては\n我\n(\nわ\n)\nが\n子\n(\nこ\n)\nはいつも\n愛\n(\nあい\n)\nする\n我\n(\nわ\n)\nが\n子\n(\nこ\n)\n。\nNo matter\nwhat, from a parent's point of view, their child is always their beloved child.\nたとえ\n小\n(\nちい\n)\nさなもの\nであれ\n検察官\n(\nけんさつかん\n)\nは\n賄賂\n(\nわいろ\n)\nを\n受\n(\nう\n)\nけ\n取\n(\nと\n)\nるわけにはいかない。\nEven if\nit is just a small thing, the public prosecutor must not accept a bribe.\nたとえ\n氷\n(\nこおり\n)\nのように\n純粋\n(\nじゅんすい\n)\nであれ\n、\n世界\n(\nせかい\n)\nの\n悪\n(\nあく\n)\nからは\n免\n(\nまぬが\n)\nれられないだろう。\nEven if\none is as pure as ice, it seems that one cannot avoid the evil of the world.\nGet more example sentences!\nPremium users get access to 12 example sentences on all Grammar Points.\nTry Bunpro\nSelf-Study Sentences\nStudy your own way!\nAdd sentences and study them alongside Bunpro sentences.\nTry Bunpro\nOnline\nBreakdown, comparisons, and examples\nJLPT先生\nCommon usages and examples\nJGram\nOffline\nA Dictionary of Advanced Japanese Grammar\nPage 67\nTrack Resources!\nBunpro tracks all of the resources you’ve visited, and offers relevant bookmarks of physical books to help with offline tracking.\nTry Bunpro\nであれ – Grammar Discussion\nMost Recent Replies (1 in total)\ndomi650\nI don´t understand the difference in usage between であれ and  であろうと.\nAnd if I see it correctly, it doesn´t get explained at all in this grammar point.\nIt just says to place them after a noun or WH-Word, but in the reviews であろうと gets marked as yellow/wrong and Bunpro tells you to use であれ instead?\nI first thought maybe it´s the case that であろうと comes after Na-Adjectives and であれ after Nouns, however, this is disproven as both come after normal Nouns in the example sentences. It seems to be a nuance in meaning and usage as the であろうと uses the volitional form, but without explanations I can only speculate…\nIt seems like you planned this grammar point exclusively for であれ and added であろうと as a similar alternative without any explanations\nPlease add something there, Bunpro\nGot questions about であれ?\nJoin us to discuss, ask, and learn together!\nJoin the Discussion\nBunpro\nSimplifying Japanese\nOfficial Apps\nLearn More\nJoin us!\nCompany\nNews\nCareers\nAbout Us\nTestimonials\nAcknowledgements\nFor Teachers\nJapanese\nOfficial Forums\nContent Search\nReading Practice\nGrammar Library\nHiragana & Katakana\nSupport\nContact Us\nSupport & FAQ\n© 2026, Bunpro SRS.\nRead our\nTerms of Service\n,\nPrivacy Policy\nand\nCompany Overview\n.\nMade with\n❤️\nfrom Osaka.\nEnglish",
