      "sourceText": "なくして(は) (JLPT N1) | Bunpro\nLoading user data...\nBunpro\nGrammar Info\nN1 Lesson 5: 7/18\nなくしては\nWithout, If not for\nDetails\nExamples\nResources\nなくして(は)\nWithout, If not for\nDetails\nExamples\nResources\nDetails\nExamples\nResources\nReady to transform your studies?\nLearn N5 in under a month!\nTry now, no credit card required!\nTry Bunpro\nLearn More\nStructure\nNoun +\nなくして\n(\nは\n)\nVerb +\nことなくして\n(\nは\n)\nDetails\nRegister\nFormal\nAbout なくして(は)\nEnglish\nJapanese\nなくしては\nis a hypothetical expression that indicates that 'if not for (A), then not (B)'. It may appear as either なしには, なしでは, or\nなくしては\n, with little variation in meaning. It is a combination of the\nconjunctive form\nof the い-Adjective ない, なく, the\nconjunction particle\nして, which highlights the word before it as a condition from which a determination can be made, and the\nadverbial particle\nは.\nAs the second part of\nなくしては\nsentences will also be negative, we can see the more literal meaning of 'from the lack of (A), a lack of (B) can be determined'. This 'determination' comes across quite strongly, and may be interpreted as '(B) is impossible without (A)'.\nなくしては\nwill appear after either nouns, or phrases that have been nominalized with こと.\nAs mentioned previously,\nなしには\nand\nなしでは\nmay also be seen. These are just the\nnoun\n無\n(\nな\n)\nし 'without', paired with either of the particle combinations には or では.\nなくしては\nis the most formal of the three.\nThe (B) part of\nなくしては\nsentences will almost always be some state of completion or desirable outcome that cannot be achieved without (A).\nSynonyms\nExpand All\n抜きで\nぬきで\nWithout, Unless\nN2 Grammar\nWhile both of these expressions convey a sense of 'without (this)', they can differ in what follows. 抜きで is used in a general sense over many contexts to mean 'without/unless', while なくして(は) is typically followed by some state of completion (usually a positive/desirable one), that cannot be achieved without the presence/condition given.\nVocab Coverage\nAll Bunpro Vocab that appears on this item.\nExpand List\nKnowledge Check\nExamples\n--:--\nSentence\nTranslation\n名言\n(\nめいげん\n)\n：「\n努力\n(\nどりょく\n)\nなくして\n成功\n(\nせいこう\n)\nなし。」\nWise saying\n: 'There is no success\nwithout\nhard work.'\n愛\n(\nあい\n)\nなくしては\n生\n(\nい\n)\nきられないというが、それが\n苦痛\n(\nくつう\n)\nになることもある。\nThey say that one cannot live\nwithout\nlove, but sometimes it becomes a significant burden.\nトランジスタの\n開発\n(\nかいはつ\n)\nなくして\n、\n現在\n(\nげんざい\n)\nの\n世界\n(\nせかい\n)\nは\n成立\n(\nせいりつ\n)\nしえない。\nThe world we know today is not possible\nwithout\nthe development of transistors.\n「ノーベル\n賞\n(\nしょう\n)\n受賞\n(\nじゅしょう\n)\nはノーベル\n委員会\n(\nいいんかい\n)\nに\n是認\n(\nぜにん\n)\nされる\nことなくしては\n、ありえないことであろう。」\nReceiving the Nobel prize is impossible\nwithout\nthe approval of the Nobel Committee.\nスピーチ、\nＣＥＯ\n(\nシーイーオー\n)\n：「\n消費者\n(\nしょうひしゃ\n)\nの\n皆様\n(\nみなさま\n)\nとの\n協力\n(\nきょうりょく\n)\nなくしては\nこの\n商品\n(\nしょうひん\n)\n開発\n(\nかいはつ\n)\nは\n不可能\n(\nふかのう\n)\nであります。」\nSpeech, CEO\n: 'The development of this product is impossible\nwithout\nthe cooperation of all of our consumers.'\nGet more example sentences!\nPremium users get access to 12 example sentences on all Grammar Points.\nTry Bunpro\nSelf-Study Sentences\nStudy your own way!\nAdd sentences and study them alongside Bunpro sentences.\nTry Bunpro\nOnline\nBreakdown, examples, and audio\nJapaneseTest4You\nOffline\nA Dictionary of Advanced Japanese Grammar\nPage 315\nShin Kanzen Master N1 Bunpou\nPage 43\nSou Matome Bunpou N1\nPage 62\nTry N1\nPage 168\nTrack Resources!\nBunpro tracks all of the resources you’ve visited, and offers relevant bookmarks of physical books to help with offline tracking.\nTry Bunpro\nなくして(は) – Grammar Discussion\nThere's currently no discussion for なくして(は)\nAsk questions and learn together with other Bunpro users!\nJoin the Discussion\nBunpro\nSimplifying Japanese\nOfficial Apps\nLearn More\nJoin us!\nCompany\nNews\nCareers\nAbout Us\nTestimonials\nAcknowledgements\nFor Teachers\nJapanese\nOfficial