      "sourceText": "を皮切りに (JLPT N1) | Bunpro\nLoading user data...\nBunpro\nGrammar Info\nN1 Lesson 2: 4/18\nを\n皮切\n(\nかわき\n)\nりに\nBeginning of, Starting with\nDetails\nExamples\nResources\nを皮切りに\nBeginning of, Starting with\nDetails\nExamples\nResources\nDetails\nExamples\nResources\nReady to transform your studies?\nLearn N5 in under a month!\nTry now, no credit card required!\nTry Bunpro\nLearn More\nStructure\nNoun +\nを\n皮切\n(\nかわき\n)\nりにして\n(1)\nVerb［る］\n(2)\n+\nの\n+\nを\n皮切\n(\nかわき\n)\nりにして\n(1)\n(1)\nを\n皮切\n(\nかわき\n)\nりとして\n(2)\nVerb［た］\nDetails\nRegister\nStandard\nAbout を皮切りに\nEnglish\nJapanese\nを\n皮切\n(\nかわき\n)\nりに\nis a grammar structure that will be utilized with nouns in order to show the starting point for something, from which it then expanded, or something kept happening after. In most cases,\nを\n皮切\n(\nかわき\n)\nりに\nwill just be translated as 'starting with (A)', or 'beginning with (A)'.\nThis structure is a combination of the\nadverbial particle\nを, the noun\n皮切\n(\nかわき\n)\nり 'beginning' or 'outset', and the case-marking particle に. It will appear after nouns or phrases that have been nominalized, before going on to explain how something continued to expand afterwards.\nIn place of に by itself, にして and として are also standard variations of the same grammar pattern.\nCaution\nIt is rare for\nを\n皮切\n(\nかわき\n)\nりに\nto be used in relation to natural phenomena, or negative results. What happens as a result of (A) will usually be something positive, and have a specific 'doer'.\nFun Fact\nAlthough\n皮切\n(\nかわき\n)\nり is really only used to mean 'beginning', the kanji combination of 'to cut a hide' can be used as a helpful memory tool for the nuance of creating a starting point from which something expanded outwards over a large area, like skinning an animal.\nRelated\nExpand All\nをはじめ\nをはじめ\nNot only...but also..., Starting with\nN3 Grammar\nを皮切りに marks the beginning of a sequence of events, e.g. 東京公演を皮切りに全国ツアーが始まった ('With the Tokyo performance as the start, their national tour began'). をはじめ lists a representative example from a group, focusing on inclusion rather than sequence, e.g. 田中先生をはじめ、皆さんに感謝している ('Beginning with Prof. Tanaka, I'm grateful to everyone').\nVocab Coverage\nAll Bunpro Vocab that appears on this item.\nExpand List\nKnowledge Check\nExamples\n--:--\nSentence\nTranslation\n店\n(\nみせ\n)\nの\n移転\n(\nいてん\n)\nを\n皮切\n(\nかわき\n)\nりとして\n、\n売上\n(\nうりあ\n)\nげがどんどんと\n上\n(\nあ\n)\nがっています。\nStarting with\nthe shop relocation, sales are rapidly increasing.\nそれ\nを\n皮切\n(\nかわき\n)\nりとして\n、コンビニは\n相次\n(\nあいつ\n)\nいで\n出店\n(\nしゅってん\n)\nし\n始\n(\nはじ\n)\nめた。\nStarting with\nthat, convenience stores started opening one after the other.\n俳優\n(\nはいゆう\n)\nの\n伝記\n(\nでんき\n)\n：「『\nＹ\n(\nワイ\n)\n-\nＭＥＮ\n(\nメン\n)\n』に\n出演\n(\nしゅつえん\n)\nした\nのを\n皮切\n(\nかわき\n)\nりにして\n、\n多数\n(\nたすう\n)\n出演\n(\nしゅつえん\n)\n。」\nActor's biography\n: '\nStarting with\nhis appearance in\nY-MEN\nhe appeared in numerous performances.'\n皆川\n(\nみながわ\n)\nさんが\n監督\n(\nかんとく\n)\nとして\n選\n(\nえら\n)\nばれた\nのを\n皮切\n(\nかわき\n)\nりにして\n、うちのチームは\n次々\n(\nつぎつぎ\n)\nとスポーツの\n成功\n(\nせいこう\n)\nを\n掴\n(\nつか\n)\nんだ。\nStarting with\nMinagawa-san being chosen as our trainer, our team continued to be successful.\n「レオナルド・ディカプリオはタイタニックの\n主人公\n(\nしゅじんこう\n)\nになった\nのを\n皮切\n(\nかわき\n)\nりにして\nスターへの\n道\n(\nみち\n)\nを\n歩\n(\nあゆ\n)\nみ\n始\n(\nはじ\n)\nめ、\n大\n(\nだい\n)\nヒット\n映画\n(\nえいが\n)\nに\n出演\n(\nしゅつえん\n)\nしている。」\n'\nStarting with\nhis leading role in\nTitanic\n, Leonardo DiCaprio embarked on the road to stardom and has appeared in many hit movies.'\nGet more example sentences!\nPremium users get access to 12 example sentences on all Grammar Points.\nTry Bunpro\nSelf-Study Sentences\nStudy your own way!\nAdd sentences and study them alongside Bunpro sentences.\nTry Bunpro\nOnline\nAdditional information and examples\nJGram\nBreakdown and examples\nJapaneseTest4You\nGrammar notes and examples\nJLPT 先生\n接続・意味・使い方\n日本語教師のN1et\nOffline\nThere are no Offline resources listed for 「を皮切りに」.\nYou can\nsubmit a resource for review\n. Resources are constantly updated, come back later to see new additions!\nTrack Resources!\nBunpro tracks all of the resources you’ve visited, and offers relevant bookmarks of physical books to help with offline tracking.\nTry Bunpro\nを皮切りに – Grammar Discussion\nThere's currently no discussion for を皮切りに\nAsk questions and learn together with other Bunpro users!\nJoin the Discussion\nBunpro\nSimplifying Japanese\nOfficial Apps\nLearn More\nJoin us!\nCompany\nNews\nCareers\nAbout Us\nTestimonials\nAcknowledgements\nFor Teachers\nJapanese\nOfficial Forums\nContent Search\nReading Practice\nGrammar Library\nHiragana & Katakana\nSupport\nContact Us\nSupport & FAQ\n© 2026, Bunpro SRS.\nRead our\nTerms of Service\n,\nPrivacy Policy\nand\nCompany Overview\n.\nMade with\n❤️\nfrom Osaka.\nEnglish",
