      "sourceText": "に即して (JLPT N1) | Bunpro\nLoading user data...\nBunpro\nGrammar Info\nN1 Lesson 8: 15/20\nに\n即\n(\nそく\n)\nして\nIn line with, Based on, In accordance with\nDetails\nExamples\nResources\nに即して\nIn line with, Based on, In accordance with\nDetails\nExamples\nResources\nDetails\nExamples\nResources\nReady to transform your studies?\nLearn N5 in under a month!\nTry now, no credit card required!\nTry Bunpro\nLearn More\nStructure\nNoun +\nに\n即\n(\nそく\n)\nし\n(1)\n（て）\nNoun +\nに\n即\n(\nそく\n)\nした\n(1)\n+ Noun\n(1)\nに\n則\n(\nそく\n)\nした\nDetails\nRegister\nFormal\nAbout に即して\nEnglish\nJapanese\nに\n即\n(\nそく\n)\nして\nis a formal grammar structure which is used to express that something is being done for the purpose of handling a matter in the best possible way. It is a combination of に, and the する-verb\n即\n(\nそく\n)\nする 'in accordance with (A)', ' in line with (A)' in its て-form. Occasionally,\nに\n則\n(\nそく\n)\nして\n'in following with' will be used instead.\nThis structure will be used before nouns, or may be used when one noun is directly modifying another. In the case of the latter,\nに\n即\n(\nそく\n)\nした\nwill be used instead of\nに\n即\n(\nそく\n)\nして\n.\nCaution\nに\n即\n(\nそく\n)\nして\nis used when things are being done based on circumstances or situations, while\nに\n則\n(\nそく\n)\nして\ntends to be used when something is being done in accordance with laws, policies, or standards. There are situations where\nに\n則\n(\nそく\n)\nして\nwill be incorrect, so\nに\n即\n(\nそく\n)\nして\nis often used in both cases in recent years.\nRelated\nExpand All\nに則って・に則り\nにのっとって\nAccording to, In accordance with, Based on, In line with\nN1 Grammar\nBoth mean ‘based on/in accordance with,’ but the nuance differs slightly. に即して emphasizes adapting closely to actual conditions, facts, or the current situation, often suggesting flexibility or responsiveness, as in 現状に即して判断する ('Make a decision based on the current situation.'). に則って・に則り is more formal and rule-oriented, meaning ‘in accordance with’ established standards, rules, or principles, as in 規則に則って手続きを進める ('Proceed with the procedure in accordance with the rules.').\nVocab Coverage\nAll Bunpro Vocab that appears on this item.\nExpand List\nKnowledge Check\nExamples\n--:--\nSentence\nTranslation\n映画\n(\nえいが\n)\nは\n実情\n(\nじつじょう\n)\nに\n即\n(\nそく\n)\nして\n制作\n(\nせいさく\n)\nされたものだ。\nThe movie was made\nin line\nwith actual circumstances.\n経済\n(\nけいざい\n)\n状況\n(\nじょうきょう\n)\nに\n即\n(\nそく\n)\nして\n課税\n(\nかぜい\n)\nを\n調整\n(\nちょうせい\n)\nする\n必要\n(\nひつよう\n)\nがある。\nThere is a need to adjust taxes\nin line with\nthe economic condition.\n役職\n(\nやくしょく\n)\nに\n関\n(\nかか\n)\nわらず、ルール\nに\n即\n(\nそく\n)\nして\n平等\n(\nびょうどう\n)\nに\n罰\n(\nばっ\n)\nせられるべきだ。\nRegardless of position, punishment ought to be given equally,\nin line with\nthe rules.\n現実\n(\nげんじつ\n)\nに\n即\n(\nそく\n)\nして\n撮\n(\nと\n)\nられたホラー\n系\n(\nけい\n)\nのドキュメンタリーほど\n怖\n(\nこわ\n)\nいものはありません。\nThere is nothing scarier than horror documentaries that are shot\nbased on\ntrue events.\nＭｃＲｏｎａｌｄ\n(\nマクロナルド\n)\n社\n(\nしゃ\n)\nと\nＳＦＣ\n(\nエスエフシー\n)\n社\n(\nしゃ\n)\nとの\n抗争\n(\nこうそう\n)\nは\n現地\n(\nげんち\n)\nの\n法律\n(\nほうりつ\n)\nに\n即\n(\nそく\n)\nして\n処理\n(\nしょり\n)\nされる。\nThe dispute between McRonald and SFC will be handled\nin line with\nlocal law.\nGet more example sentences!\nPremium users get access to 12 example sentences on all Grammar Points.\nTry Bunpro\nSelf-Study Sentences\nStudy your own way!\nAdd sentences and study them alongside Bunpro sentences.\nTry Bunpro\nOnline\nBased On\nImabi\nに即して\nJapaneseTest4You\nOffline\nShin Kanzen Master N1 Bunpou\nPage 94\nSou Matome Bunpou N1\nPage 95\nTry N1\nPage 61\nTrack Resources!\nBunpro tracks all of the resources you’ve visited, and offers relevant bookmarks of physical books to help with offline tracking.\nTry Bunpro\nに即して – Grammar Discussion\nThere's currently no discussion for に即して\nAsk questions and learn together with other Bunpro users!\nJoin the Discussion\nBunpro\nSimplifying Japanese\nOfficial Apps\nLearn More\nJoin us!\nCompany\nNews\nCareers\nAbout Us\nT