      "sourceText": "を経て (JLPT N1) | Bunpro\nLoading user data...\nBunpro\nGrammar Info\nN1 Lesson 3: 4/18\nを\n経\n(\nへ\n)\nて\nVia, Through, After (experience at job, university, etc.), Pass through\nDetails\nExamples\nResources\nを経て\nVia, Through, After (experience at job, university, etc.), Pass through\nDetails\nExamples\nResources\nDetails\nExamples\nResources\nReady to transform your studies?\nLearn N5 in under a month!\nTry now, no credit card required!\nTry Bunpro\nLearn More\nStructure\nNoun +\nを\n経\n(\nへ\n)\nて\nDetails\nRegister\nFormal\nAbout を経て\nEnglish\nJapanese\nを\n経\n(\nへ\n)\nて\nis a fairly formal grammar point used when highlighting a passage of time, or an event that took a certain amount of time.\n経\n(\nへ\n)\nる itself is a る-Verb that means 'to elapse' or 'to pass' in terms of time. The difference between it and\n過\n(\nす\n)\nぎる 'to pass time' is that\n過\n(\nす\n)\nぎる focuses on having reached the end point, while\n経\n(\nへ\n)\nる focuses on what was happening for the whole period leading up to that end point. Because of this,\nを\n経\n(\nへ\n)\nて\ncan also be translated as 'having undergone (A)', due to the emphasis being on the preceding action.\nを\n経\n(\nへ\n)\nて\nwill directly follow nouns, and the rest of the sentence usually then goes on to describe the significance of that passage of time or experience, or what happened as a result.\nAs it is a formal structure,\nを\n経\n(\nへ\n)\nて\nis often seen in biographies, introductions, and similar media.\nRelated\nExpand All\nを通じて・を通して\nをつうじて\nThrough, Via, Throughout\nN2 Grammar\nThese are both formal expressions that use the て form of a verb to express the idea of 'through' or 'after'. を経て (as might be expected from its derivation from the verb\n経る\n(\nへる\n)\n’to pass’ or\n経つ\n(\nたつ\n)\n‘to pass (specifically of time)’ can be used with time expressions, e.g. 2年の交際を経て結婚しました ('They got married after a two-year relationship.'). In contrast, を通じて・を通して can be used for experiences or other avenues that do not necessarily imply a passage of time, e.g. 弁護士を通じて相手に連絡する 'contact someone through a lawyer'.\nVocab Coverage\nAll Bunpro Vocab that appears on this item.\nExpand List\nKnowledge Check\nExamples\n--:--\nSentence\nTranslation\nベルリンからローマ\nを\n経\n(\nへ\n)\nて\nブエノスアイレスに\n向\n(\nむ\n)\nかいます。\nFrom Berlin,\nvia\nRome, to Buenos Aires. (\nthrough\n)\n数\n(\nすう\n)\n世代\n(\nせだい\n)\nを\n経\n(\nへ\n)\nても\nなお\n争議\n(\nそうぎ\n)\nが\n続\n(\nつづ\n)\nいている。\nEven after\nseveral generations, the dispute still continues. (\nthrough・via・experience\n)\nちとげとらくは、\n約\n(\nやく\n)\n１０\n(\nじゅう\n)\n年\n(\nねん\n)\nの\n交際\n(\nこうさい\n)\nを\n経\n(\nへ\n)\nて\n結婚\n(\nけっこん\n)\nした。\nChitoge and Raku finally married\nafter going through\nabout ten years of dating. (\nthrough・via・experience\n)\n略歴\n(\nりゃくれき\n)\n：「\n早稲田大学\n(\nわせだだいがく\n)\n理学部\n(\nりがくぶ\n)\n卒業後\n(\nそつぎょうご\n)\nＧｏｏｇｌｅ\n(\nグーグル\n)\n勤務\n(\nきんむ\n)\nを\n経\n(\nへ\n)\nて\n２０\n(\nにせん\n)\n２\n(\nにー\n)\n〇\n(\nまる\n)\n年\n(\nねん\n)\n独立\n(\nどくりつ\n)\n。」\nShort bio\n: 'Graduated from the department of science, Waseda University.\nAfter (having the experience of)\nworking at Google, he started his own business in 202X.' (\nthrough・via\n)\n新聞\n(\nしんぶん\n)\n：「\n今後\n(\nこんご\n)\n必要\n(\nひつよう\n)\nな\n手続\n(\nてつづ\n)\nき\nを\n経\n(\nへ\n)\nて\n、\n鉱山\n(\nこうざん\n)\n買収\n(\nばいしゅう\n)\nは\n完了\n(\nかんりょう\n)\nします。」\nNewspaper\n: '\nAfter going through\nall of the necessary procedures, the mine acquisition will be complete.' (\nthrough・via・experience\n)\nGet more example sentences!\nPremium users get access to 12 example sentences on all Grammar Points.\nTry Bunpro\nSelf-Study Sentences\nStudy your own way!\nAdd sentences and study them alongside Bunpro sentences.\nTry Bunpro\nOnline\nBreakdown and examples\nJapaneseTest4You\nOffline\nShin Kanzen Master N1 Bunpou\nPage 95\nSou Matome Bunpou N1\nPage 102\nTrack Resources!\nBunpro tracks all of the resources you’ve visited, and offers relevant bookmarks of physical books to help with offline tracking.\nTry Bunpro\nを経て – Grammar Discussion\nThere's currently no discussion for を経て\nAsk questions and learn together with other Bunpro users!\nJoin the Discussion\nBunpro\nSimplifying Japanese\nOfficial Apps\nLearn More\nJoin us!\nCompany\nNews\nCareers\nAbout Us\nTestimonials\nAcknowledgements\nFor Teachers\nJapanese\nOfficial Forums\nContent Search\nReading Practice\nGrammar Library\nHiragana & Katakana\nSupport\nContact Us\nSupport & FAQ\n© 2026, Bunpro SRS.\nRead our\nTerms of Service\n,\nPrivacy Policy\nand\nCompany Overview\n.\nMade with\n❤️\nfrom Osaka.\nEnglish",
