      "sourceText": "まじき (JLPT N1) | Bunpro\nLoading user data...\nBunpro\nGrammar Info\nN1 Lesson 9: 1/20\nまじき\nUnbecoming of, Unworthy of, Not proper for, Should not, Must not, Cannot\nDetails\nExamples\nResources\nまじき\nUnbecoming of, Unworthy of, Not proper for, Should not, Must not, Cannot\nDetails\nExamples\nResources\nDetails\nExamples\nResources\nReady to transform your studies?\nLearn N5 in under a month!\nTry now, no credit card required!\nTry Bunpro\nLearn More\nStructure\nNoun (A) +\nに\nある\n(1)\n+\nまじき\n+ Noun (B)\n許すまじき\n+ Noun\n(1)\nとして\nある\nDetails\nRegister\nFormal\nAbout まじき\nEnglish\nJapanese\nまじき\nis the\nattributive form\nof まじ, a\nclassical auxiliary verb\nthat has been replaced almost entirely by まい 'must not', 'should not' in modern Japanese. まじ itself has this same meaning of 'must not', and will only be seen in a very limited number of formal expressions. Although slightly different in nuance,\nまじき\nis often translated simply as 'not proper for (A)', or 'unbecoming of (A)' in each case.\nThe most common pattern that\nまじき\nwill be seen in is (A)\nにあるまじき\n(B), where the case-marking particle に follows a noun, then is linked to the う-Verb ある, before\nまじき\nwill connect to a second noun.\nOccasionally, に will be replaced by として 'as', with the rest of the structure remaining the same.\n許\n(\nゆる\n)\nすまじき\n'must not be forgiven', or simply 'unforgivable' is another pattern that may be seen.\nRelated\nExpand All\nはずがない\nはずがない\nHardly possible, Cannot be, Highly unlikely, Improbable\nN4 Grammar\nBoth express strong denial, but their usage differs. まじき is a formal, literary expression usually found in fixed phrases such as あるまじき, and is used to judge that something is morally or socially unacceptable rather than logically impossible, as in 指導者としてあるまじき行為だ ('It is behavior unbecoming of a leader.'). はずがない denies possibility based on logic, evidence, or common sense, stating that something cannot be true, as in 彼がそんなことをするはずがない ('There is no way he would do such a thing.').\nVocab Coverage\nAll Bunpro Vocab that appears on this item.\nExpand List\nKnowledge Check\nExamples\n--:--\nSentence\nTranslation\nリヒャルトは\n王\n(\nおう\n)\nとしてあるまじき\n汚名\n(\nおめい\n)\nを\n着\n(\nき\n)\nせられ、やがて\n廃位\n(\nはいい\n)\nされた。\nRichard was tarred with the stigma\nunbecoming of\nthe position of the king and was eventually dethroned.\n言\n(\nい\n)\nうまでもないが、\n公金\n(\nこうきん\n)\n横領\n(\nおうりょう\n)\nなど\n政治家\n(\nせいじか\n)\nとしてあるまじき\n行為\n(\nこうい\n)\nだ。\nIt goes without saying, but something like misappropriation of public funds is an act\nunbecoming of\na statesman.\n妻\n(\nつま\n)\nを\n下\n(\nさ\n)\nげるような\n発言\n(\nはつげん\n)\nをするなんて、\n夫\n(\nおっと\n)\nにあるまじき\n行為\n(\nこうい\n)\nだ。\nSomething like saying remarks that bring down his wife, it is behavior that is\nunbecoming of\na husband.\n戦場\n(\nせんじょう\n)\nから\n離脱\n(\nりだつ\n)\nすることは\n武士\n(\nぶし\n)\nにあるまじき\n行為\n(\nこうい\n)\nと\n咎\n(\nとが\n)\nめられ、\n罰\n(\nばっ\n)\nせられた。\nFleeing from the battlefield was condemned as\nunbecoming of\na warrior and punished.\nララティーナは\n貴族\n(\nきぞく\n)\nにあるまじき\n態度\n(\nたいど\n)\nで、\n甘\n(\nあま\n)\nやかされた\n子供\n(\nこども\n)\nのようなふるまいをした。\nLalatina behaved in a manner\nunbecoming of\na noble, like a spoiled child.\nGet more example sentences!\nPremium users get access to 12 example sentences on all Grammar Points.\nTry Bunpro\nSelf-Study Sentences\nStudy your own way!\nAdd sentences and study them alongside Bunpro sentences.\nTry Bunpro\nOnline\nThe Volitional 2\nImabi\nまじき\nJapaneseTest4You\nまじき\nJLPTSensei\nOffline\nShin Kanzen Master N1 Bunpou\nPage 59\nSou Matome Bunpou N1\nPage 137\nTry N1\nPage 163\nTrack Resources!\nBunpro tracks all of the resources you’ve visited, and offers relevant bookmarks of physical books to help with offline tracking.\nTry Bunpro\nまじき – Grammar Discussion\nThere's currently no discussion for まじき\nAsk questions and learn together with other Bunpro users!\nJoin the Discussion\nBunpro\nSimplifying Japanese\nOfficial Apps\nLearn More\nJoin us!\nCompany\nNews\nCareers\nAbout Us\nTestimonials\nAcknowledgements