      "sourceText": "ずじまい (JLPT N1) | Bunpro\nLoading user data...\nBunpro\nGrammar Info\nN1 Lesson 9: 4/20\nずじまい\nEnded up not, Did not (in the end), Never did\noriginates from the voiced verb[stem] form of しまう. Very often used in past form.\nDetails\nExamples\nResources\nずじまい\nEnded up not, Did not (in the end), Never did\nDetails\nExamples\nResources\nDetails\nExamples\nResources\nReady to transform your studies?\nLearn N5 in under a month!\nTry now, no credit card required!\nTry Bunpro\nLearn More\nStructure\nVerb［\nない\n］\n+\nず\n+\nじまい\nDetails\nRegister\nStandard\nAbout ずじまい\nEnglish\nJapanese\nずじまい\nis a grammar structure that combines the literary form of the\nclassical auxiliary verb\nぬ, ず 'not', and the voiced\nconjunctive form\nof the う-Verb しまう 'to finish', or 'to bring to a close', じまい. Like しまう, ずじまい will often indicate regret at something ending up a certain way. However, this regret is about '(A) not happening', due to the negation provided by ず.\nThis structure will be used following the\nindeterminate form\nof verbs. Common translations include 'to end up not (A)', and 'to not have done (A) in the end'.\nずじまい\nwill often be followed by だった or でした, indicating that (A) was not something that turned out happening, despite the wishes or intentions of the doer.\nCaution\nAs is always the case with ず, する will be altered to せず.\nRelated\nExpand All\nまま(に)\nままに (As Is)\nAs is, While remaining, Left in a state\nN3 Grammar\nBoth relate to a state continuing without change. まま describes a condition or state that remains as it is, neutral in tone, and when used as ないまま it means an action did not happen and that non-action continued, as in 行かないままだった ('I remained in a state of not going.'). ずじまい is especially close to ないまま but emphasizes the outcome that, after time or circumstances, the action never happened at all, often with regret or resignation, as in 結局行かずじまいだった ('In the end, I never went.').\nVocab Coverage\nAll Bunpro Vocab that appears on this item.\nExpand List\nKnowledge Check\nExamples\n--:--\nSentence\nTranslation\nＡ\n(\nエー\n)\n：「\n結局\n(\nけっきょく\n)\n、\nやらずじまい\nで\n新\n(\nしん\n)\n学期\n(\nがっき\n)\nになっちゃった\nよ\n。」\nＢ\n(\nビー\n)\n：「なにをやらなかったの？」\nＡ\n(\nエー\n)\n：「\n夏休\n(\nなつやす\n)\nみ\nの\n宿題\n(\nしゅくだい\n)\n…」\nA\n: 'I\nended up not\ndoing it, and the new school term started.'\nB\n: 'What did you not do?'\nA\n: 'The summer homework...'\n「\n宇崎\n(\nうざき\n)\nさんと\n映画館\n(\nえいがかん\n)\nに\n行\n(\nい\n)\nこうと\n思\n(\nおも\n)\nっていたけど、\n仕事\n(\nしごと\n)\nから\n手\n(\nて\n)\nが\n離\n(\nはな\n)\nせなくて\n結局\n(\nけっきょく\n)\n行\n(\nい\n)\nけずじまい\nだった。」\n'I planned to go to the cinema with Uzaki, but I couldn't get away from work, so I\nended up not\ngoing.'\n小説\n(\nしょうせつ\n)\n：「\n事故\n(\nじこ\n)\nの\n原因\n(\nげんいん\n)\nについて\n調\n(\nしら\n)\nべようとしたが、ついに\nわからずじまい\nだった。」\nNovel\n: 'I tried to investigate the cause of the accident, but I\nended up not\ndiscovering anything.'\n「\n最新\n(\nさいしん\n)\nの\n愛\n(\nあい\n)\nＰｈｏｎｅ\n(\nフォン\n)\nを\n買\n(\nか\n)\nおうとストアに\n１０\n(\nじゅう\n)\n時間\n(\nじかん\n)\n並\n(\nなら\n)\nんだのに、\n自分\n(\nじぶん\n)\nの\n番\n(\nばん\n)\nが\n来\n(\nく\n)\nる\n頃\n(\nころ\n)\nには\n欲\n(\nほ\n)\nしい\n色\n(\nいろ\n)\nがもう\n売\n(\nう\n)\nり\n切\n(\nき\n)\nれていて\n結局\n(\nけっきょく\n)\n買\n(\nか\n)\nえずじまい\nだった。」\n'I stood for 10 hours in line to buy the new 愛Phone, but when my turn came, it turned out that the color I wanted had already sold out, so I\nended up not buying\nit.'\n「\n日本語\n(\nにほんご\n)\nの\n教科書\n(\nきょうかしょ\n)\nをたくさん\n買\n(\nか\n)\nったけど、\n結局\n(\nけっきょく\n)\n使\n(\nつか\n)\nわずじまい\nだった。」\n'I bought lots of Japanese textbooks, but I\nended up not\nusing them.'\nGet more example sentences!\nPremium users get access to 12 example sentences on all Grammar Points.\nTry Bunpro\nSelf-Study Sentences\nStudy your own way!\nAdd sentences and study them alongside Bunpro sentences.\nTry Bunpro\nOnline\nずじまい\nJapaneseTest4You\nOffline\nShin Kanzen Master N2 Bunpou\nPage 91\nTrack Resources!\nBunpro tracks all of the resources you’ve visited, and offers relevant bookmarks of physical books to help with offline tracking.\nTry Bunpro\nずじまい – Grammar Discussion\nThere's currently no discussion for ずじまい\nAsk questions and learn together with other Bunpro users!\nJoin the Discussion\nBunpro\nSimplifying Japanese\nOfficial Apps\nLearn More\nJoin us!\nCompany\nNews\nCareers\nAbout Us\nTestimonials\nAcknowledgements\nFor Teachers\nJapanese\nOfficial Forums\nContent Search\nReading Practice\nGrammar Library\nHiragana & Katakana\nSupport\nContact Us\nSupport & FAQ\n© 2026, Bunpro SRS.\nRead our\nTerms of Service\n,\nPrivacy Policy\nand\nCompany Overview\n.\nMade with\n❤️\nfrom Osaka.\nEnglish",
