      "sourceText": "だ (JLPT N5) | Bunpro\nLoading user data...\nBunpro\nGrammar Info\nN5 Lesson 1: 1/12\nだ\nTo be, Is\nだ cannot be used with い-Adjectives\nDetails\nExamples\nResources\nだ\nTo be, Is\nDetails\nExamples\nResources\nDetails\nExamples\nResources\nReady to transform your studies?\nLearn N5 in under a month!\nTry now, no credit card required!\nTry Bunpro\nLearn More\nStructure\nNoun +\nだ\n［な］Adjective\n+\nだ\nDetails\nPart of Speech\nAuxiliary Verb\nWord Type\nDependent Word\nRegister\nStandard\nAbout だ\nFor the most part,\nだ\nis the equivalent of 'is' in English. Its role is to strongly express determination or assertion. It is a casual grammar structure, which means that you won't see it in polite sentences.\nTechnically,\nだ\nis an\nauxiliary verb\n, a group of words that attach themselves to other words to give them meaning.\nです\nhas the same role as\nだ\n, but\nです\nis the one that will be used in polite sentences, and is also one of the first Japanese grammar patterns many people are exposed to.\nだ\nwill always follow nouns, or words that behave like nouns, such as\nな-Adjectives\n.\nCaution\nAlthough\nです\n, the polite equivalent of\nだ\n, can be seen following\nい-Adjectives\n,\nだ\nitself will never be used directly after an\nい-Adjective\n.\nCaution\nWhile\nだ\nis often thought of as the 'casual form' of\nです\n, that is actually not entirely true.\nです\nis a\npolite speech\nword. The official 'formal version' of\nだ\nis\nである\n. We will learn this grammar point a bit later.\nである\ncan often be seen in articles, and formal writing, while\nです\nis more common in\npolite speech\n.\nTopics\nWelcome to Bunpro! 文プロへようこそ！\nN5 Topic\nWelcome to the start of the Bunpro learning path! The goal of this first Topic is to learn how to make declarative statements using the Japanese equivalents of ‘is’. This is fundamental to almost any language, and is achieved in Japanese through the use of だ and です.\n2m\nSynonyms\nExpand All\nです\nTo be, Is\nN5 Grammar\nだ and です both function like the English 'is.' The main difference is politeness: だ is casual and used in plain speech, while です is polite. だ can't be used after い-adjectives, but です can, acting as a general politeness marker. You may still see だ in set expressions like ～だと思います, even in polite sentences.\nである\nFormal or literary だ, Authoritative, Copula\nN3 Grammar\nThe main difference between だ and である is formality. だ is casual and common in conversation, while である is more formal and mainly used in writing. Both だ and である follow nouns or noun phrases, but である has a more literary tone. である slight differs from the verb ある (to exist) in that である is a fixed connector.\nでございます\nでございます\nTo be, Polite copula\nN4 Grammar\nだ conveys a casual, informal, or blunt tone, except when required by certain grammatical patterns. In contrast, でございます is a highly polite form, primarily used in business settings or when addressing someone of higher social status such as a boss or customer.\nAntonyms\nExpand All\nじゃない\nIs not, Isn't\nN5 Grammar\nだ follows nouns and な-adjectives, with a meaning similar to the English 'is.' For instance, これはペンだ translates to 'This is a pen.' On the other hand, じゃない (a contraction of ではない) is used to create the negative of such expressions. For example, これはペンじゃない translates to 'This isn't a pen.'\nRelated\nExpand All\nだった・でした\nWas, Were (Past tense)\nN5 Grammar\nだった・でした and だ are all used to assert or identify something. The difference among them is in formality and tense. だ is casual and present tense (similar to the English 'is'/'am'), while だった・でした is past tense ('was'), with だった being casual (the past tense of だ) and でした being polite (the past tense of です).\nがある\nがある\nTo be, There is\nN5 Grammar\nがある indicates the existence or possession of something. For example, ペンがある means 'There is a pen (on the table, etc.)' or 'I have a pen.' On the other hand, だ expresses assertion or determination similar to 'is/are' in English. In contrast to the がある example, ペンだ would mean 'It (=the thing we are looking at) is a pen.'\nよ\nEmphasis (Sentence ending particle)\nN5 Grammar\nよ is a common sentence-ending particle used to add emphasis, often indicating the speaker is sharing new information (e.g., 面白いよ = 'It's interesting, I'm telling you!'). だ is a grammatical form expressing assertion, similar to 'is' or 'am.' These two are often combined, especially in casual or masculine speech (元気だよ = 'I'm feeling good!'). In softer or more feminine speech, the だ is frequently omitted (e.g., 元気よ).\nVocab Coverage\nAll Bunpro Vocab that appears on this item.\nExpand List\nKnowledge Check\nExamples\n--:--\nSentence\nTranslation\n私\n(\nわたし\n)\nだ\n。\nIt\nis\nme.\n本\n(\nほん\n)\nだ\n。\nIt\nis\na book.\n猫\n(\nねこ\n)\nだ\n。\n(It)\nis\na cat.\n学生\n(\nがくせい\n)\nだ\n。\n(I)\nam\na student.\n綺麗\n(\nきれい\n)\nだ\n。\nIt\nis\nbeautiful.\nGet more example sentences!\nPremium users get access to 12 example sentences on all Grammar Points.\nTry Bunpro\nSelf-Study Sentences\nStudy your own way!\nAdd sentences and study them alongside Bunpro sentences.\nTry Bunpro\nOnline\nDeclaring something is so and so using 「だ」\nTae Kim\nThe copula だ\nAn Introduction to Japanese\nだ cannot be used with い-Adjectives\nTae Kim\nOffline\nTae Kim's Japanese Grammar Guide\nPage 29\nみんなの日本語 I\nPage 14 [CH 1]\nみんなの日本語 I\nPage 128 [CH 20]\nTrack Resources!\nBunpro tracks all of the resources you’ve visited, and offers relevant bookmarks of physical books to help with offline tracking.\nTry Bunpro\nだ – Grammar Discussion\nMost Recent Replies (1 in total)\nPythonMaxmarian_67\nIMPORTANT NOTE REGARDING THE USE OF THIS GRAMMAR:\nJapanese Textbooks may have provided you with this explanation regarding the use of these 2 variants, だ is casual and です is polite. However, this often-taught standard is disregarded in real Japanese everyday life. The focus of だ and です is on the reliance of social space, establishing a personal bubble where only you is inside, while others are outside.\nFor a complete understanding of this grammar, please access this Tofugu web application, which will direct you to an article regarding the real-life use of this grammar.\nTofugu – 24 ...\nGot questions about だ?\nJoin us to discuss, ask, and learn together!\nJoin the Discussion\nBunpro\nSimplifying Japanese\nOfficial Apps\nLearn More\nJoin us!\nCompany\nNews\nCareers\nAbout Us\nTestimonials\nAcknowledgements\nFor Teachers\nJapanese\nOfficial Forums\nContent Search\nReading Practice\nGrammar Library\nHiragana & Katakana\nSupport\nContact Us\nSupport & FAQ\n© 2026, Bunpro SRS.\nRead our\nTerms of Service\n,\nPrivacy Policy\nand\nCompany Overview\n.\nMade with\n❤️\nfrom Osaka.\nEnglish",
