      "sourceText": "から (JLPT N5) | Bunpro\nLoading user data...\nBunpro\nGrammar Info\nN5 Lesson 5: 4/12\nから\nFrom\nDetails\nExamples\nResources\nから\nFrom\nDetails\nExamples\nResources\nDetails\nExamples\nResources\nReady to transform your studies?\nLearn N5 in under a month!\nTry now, no credit card required!\nTry Bunpro\nLearn More\nStructure\nStarting Point +\nから\nDetails\nPart of Speech\nParticle\nWord Type\nCase Marking Particle\nRegister\nStandard\nAbout から\nから\ncan have several different meanings in Japanese, depending on which part of the sentence it is in, and what comes before/after it. It is often translated as 'from'. In these cases, it just means 'with (A) as a starting location, (B)'. In this grammar construction,\nから\ncomes directly after the place that is considered the starting point.\nThis form of\nから\nis the closest to the 'base' meaning of the word in Japanese, as the nuance of\nから\ncan almost always be thought of as meaning 'from' in some way.\nCaution\nThis form of\nから\ndoes not require\nだ\nwhen used after nouns or\nな-Adjectives\n, as that would change the meaning to '\nbecause\n'.\nTopics\nJust Because\nN5 Topic\nIn this Topic, we're going to learn how to use the conjunctive particles ので and から to mean 'because'. We'll also learn how から can be used as a case-marking particle to show origin, meaning something like 'from'. With these, we will be able to start to string together our sentences in far more natural ways by giving reasons and justifications.\n3m\nRelated\nExpand All\nてから\n～てから\nOnce...is done, Once...happens, After doing\nN5 Grammar\nてから, combining the て form of a verb with から, expresses a sequence of actions, similar to 'A, then B' or 'after A, B' in English (e.g., 食べてから寝る = 'After I eat, I'll sleep'). It can be confused with the past tense た form plus から, which expresses a reason (e.g., 食べたから寝る = 'I ate, so I'll sleep'), focusing on cause rather than sequence.\nVocab Coverage\nAll Bunpro Vocab that appears on this item.\nExpand List\nKnowledge Check\nExamples\n--:--\nSentence\nTranslation\n駅\n(\nえき\n)\nから\nバス\nで\n来\n(\nき\n)\nた\n。\nI came\nfrom\nthe station by bus.\nアメリカ\nから\n来\n(\nき\n)\nました\n。\nI came\nfrom\nAmerica.\nこの\n靴\n(\nくつ\n)\nは\nお\n母\n(\nかあ\n)\nさん\nから\nです\n。\nThese shoes are\nfrom\nmy mom.\n学校\n(\nがっこう\n)\nから\n、パーティに\n行\n(\nい\n)\nく\n。\nTo go to the party\nfrom\nschool.\n仕事\n(\nしごと\n)\nから\n帰\n(\nかえ\n)\nる\n。\nTo return home\nfrom\nwork.\nGet more example sentences!\nPremium users get access to 12 example sentences on all Grammar Points.\nTry Bunpro\nSelf-Study Sentences\nStudy your own way!\nAdd sentences and study them alongside Bunpro sentences.\nTry Bunpro\nOnline\nParticles から and まで\nWasabi\nThe Particle から\nImabi\nOffline\n[DBJG] A Dictionary of Basic Japanese Grammar\nPage 176\nみんなの日本語 I\nPage 32 [CH 4]\nTrack Resources!\nBunpro tracks all of the resources you’ve visited, and offers relevant bookmarks of physical books to help with offline tracking.\nTry Bunpro\nから – Grammar Discussion\nMost Recent Replies (4 in total)\nmachinaeZER0\nIt feels awkward to translate２時から始まります as “It starts\nfrom\ntwo o’clock.” Obviously here から is being taught as “from,” but it feels like either this sentence should use something other than から (probably not) or it would be better served with a more natural translation like “at” (which could be right, but isn’t the translation we’re being taught). Would it make sense to revisit including this sentence as currently written/translated, or am I just a weirdo?\nKasasagi\nこの靴はお母さん\nから\nです。means “these shoes are from my mother” (my mother gave them to someone, most likely me).\nこの靴はお母さん\nの\nです。means “these shoes are my mother’s” (my mother owns them).\nKasasagi\nYou’re interpretation is correct and train of thought is completely understandable.\nI’ve heard “starts from” used in English (by native speakers) with the same meaning as から始まります. It’s a very inaccurate way of speaking, but it does account for the uncertainty involved when talking about future plans.\nGot questions about から?\nJoin us to discuss, ask, and learn together!\nJoin the Discussion\nBunpro\nSimplifying Japanese\nOfficial Apps\nLearn More\nJoin us!\nCompany\nNews\nCareers\nAbout Us\nTestimonials\nAcknowledgements\nFor Teachers\nJapanese\nOfficial Forums\nContent Search\nReading Practice\nGrammar Library\nHiragana & Katakana\nSupport\nContact Us\nSupport & FAQ\n© 2026, Bunpro SRS.\nRead our\nTerms of Service\n,\nPrivacy Policy\nand\nCompany Overview\n.\nMade with\n❤️\nfrom Osaka.\nEnglish",
