      "sourceText": "Noun + まで (JLPT N5) | Bunpro\nLoading user data...\nBunpro\nGrammar Info\nN5 Lesson 8: 5/13\nNoun + まで\nUntil, Till,  To (but no further than)\nDetails\nExamples\nResources\nNoun + まで\nUntil, Till,  To (but no further than)\nDetails\nExamples\nResources\nDetails\nExamples\nResources\nReady to transform your studies?\nLearn N5 in under a month!\nTry now, no credit card required!\nTry Bunpro\nLearn More\nStructure\nEnding Point +\nまで\nNoun +\nまで\nDetails\nPart of Speech\nNoun\nWord Type\nAdverbial Particle\nRegister\nStandard\nAbout Noun + まで\nまで\nis a particle that roughly means 'as far as'. Due to this, when used with regular nouns, or words that signify some kind of end point (a time or day), it is often translated as 'until', 'till', or 'to'.\nWhen used in relation to a place,\nまで\nfunctions similarly to\nに\n. This means that someone or something will go 'to' the place, but not any further.\nまで\nmay also be used about points in time in the past, where 'up until' would usually be used in English.\nTopics\nUntil Then\nN5 Topic\nIn this Topic, we're going to learn about the particle まで. まで generally means 'until' or 'up to'. When used directly after nouns, it functions as a case-marking particle. When being used after verbs, it acts as an adverbial particle connecting two ideas.\n3m\nSynonyms\nExpand All\nVerb + まで\nUntil (something) happens\nN5 Grammar\nThe particle まで has the core meaning of 'as far as.' With nouns, it can mean 'until' with time expressions (e.g. 月曜まで休む = 'take off until Monday') or 'up to' with locations (e.g. 駅まで送る = 'see [someone] off to the station'). When used after a plain-form verb, it means 'until A happens. For example, 友達が来るまでテレビを見ていた = 'I was watching TV until my friend came.'\nRelated\nExpand All\nまでに\nBy ~, By the time that ~, Before ~\nN4 Grammar\nThe particle まで means 'until' when used with a time expression and a verb describing an ongoing action. For example, 8時までテレビを見る means 'watch TV until 8 o'clock.' In contrast, までに means 'by' and is used to express that an action is completed before a certain time. For example, 8時までに終わる means 'finish by 8 o'clock'.\nまで\nEven, To even, To the extent of\nN4 Grammar\nThe particle まで has the core meaning of 'as far as.' It's commonly used with time expressions to mean 'until' (e.g. 月曜まで休む = 'rest until Monday') and with places to mean 'up to' or 'to (a location)' (e.g. 駅まで送る = 'see [someone] off to the station'). When used with verbs or non-location nouns, it can mean 'even' or 'as much as' (e.g. 骨まで食べる = 'eat even the bones').\nVocab Coverage\nAll Bunpro Vocab that appears on this item.\nExpand List\nKnowledge Check\nExamples\n--:--\nSentence\nTranslation\nどこ\nまで\n行\n(\nい\n)\nく\n？\nHow far will you go? (\nUntil\n)\n７\n(\nしち\n)\n時\n(\nじ\n)\nまで\nです\n。\nUntil\nseven o'clock.\nこの\nセール\nは\n金曜日\n(\nきんようび\n)\nまで\nです\n。\nThis sale lasts\nuntil\nFriday.\n朝\n(\nあさ\n)\nまで\n寝\n(\nね\n)\nました\n。\nI slept\nuntil\nmorning.\n８\n(\nはち\n)\n時\n(\nじ\n)\nまで\n、テレビ\nを\n見\n(\nみ\n)\nる\n。\nTo watch TV\nuntil\neight o'clock.\nGet more example sentences!\nPremium users get access to 12 example sentences on all Grammar Points.\nTry Bunpro\nSelf-Study Sentences\nStudy your own way!\nAdd sentences and study them alongside Bunpro sentences.\nTry Bunpro\nOnline\n「まで」\nWasabi\nThe Particle まで\nImabi\nOffline\nみんなの日本語 I\nPage 32 [CH 4]\nTrack Resources!\nBunpro tracks all of the resources you’ve visited, and offers relevant bookmarks of physical books to help with offline tracking.\nTry Bunpro\nNoun + まで – Grammar Discussion\nThere's currently no discussion for Noun + まで\nAsk questions and learn together with other Bunpro users!\nJoin the Discussion\nBunpro\nSimplifying Japanese\nOfficial Apps\nLearn More\nJoin us!\nCompany\nNews\nCareers\nAbout Us\nTestimonials\nAcknowledgements\nFor Teachers\nJapanese\nOfficial Forums\nContent Search\nReading Practice\nGrammar Library\nHiragana & Katakana\nSupport\nContact Us\nSupport & FAQ\n© 2026, Bunpro SRS.\nRead our\nTerms of Servic