      "sourceText": "てから (JLPT N5) | Bunpro\nLoading user data...\nBunpro\nGrammar Info\nN5 Lesson 7: 6/13\n～てから\nOnce...is done, Once...happens, After doing\nDetails\nExamples\nResources\nてから\nOnce...is done, Once...happens, After doing\nDetails\nExamples\nResources\nDetails\nExamples\nResources\nReady to transform your studies?\nLearn N5 in under a month!\nTry now, no credit card required!\nTry Bunpro\nLearn More\nStructure\nVerb［て］\n+\nから\nDetails\nPart of Speech\nExpression\nWord Type\nCase Marking Particle\nRegister\nStandard\nAbout てから\nIn order to specifically express that one thing happens/begins to happen after another thing,\nてから\nwill be used. This expression is regularly translated as 'once (A) happens, (B)', or 'after doing (A), (B)'.\nThe difference between\nてから\n, and the regular\nて form\nfollowed by another verb, is that\nてから\nputs more emphasis on the (A) action 'enabling' the (B) action.\nCaution\nから\ncan come after almost any form of verb.\nてから\nis the only form that translates as 'after (A), (B)'. た\nから\n, and\nるから\nwill translate closer to 'because', or 'since'.\nTopics\nて Time\nN5 Topic\nIn this Topic, we're going to learn about another way ている is used, and also about the てから pattern. With these, we'll expand how we can connect verbs and describe the world.\n4m\nRelated\nExpand All\nて初めて\n～てはじめて\nFor the first time, Not until, Only after, Only when, Only because\nN3 Grammar\nて初めて and てから both use the Verb + て form to show actions happening in sequence, but with different nuances. てから simply shows that one event happened after another, while て初めて emphasizes that the second action happened 'only after' or 'not until' meaning 'for the first time after' the previous event.\nてからというもの\n～てからというもの\nAfter, Since, Ever since then\nN1 Grammar\nてからというもの can be seen as a more emphatic, formal, and wordy version of てから. Though both mean 'after/once (A), (B)', てから is often used for even simple actions, e.g. 掃除をしてから出掛けます ('I'll go out after I clean up.'), while てからというもの will be used for more profound/meaningful statements, e.g. 娘が生まれてからというもの、人生観が変わった ('Ever since my daughter was born, my view on life changed.').\nから\nFrom\nN5 Grammar\nてから, combining the て form of a verb with から, expresses a sequence of actions, similar to 'A, then B' or 'after A, B' in English (e.g., 食べてから寝る = 'After I eat, I'll sleep'). It can be confused with the past tense た form plus から, which expresses a reason (e.g., 食べたから寝る = 'I ate, so I'll sleep'), focusing on cause rather than sequence.\nVerb + て\n～て (Conjunction)\nAnd, Then (Linking events)\nN5 Grammar\nThe Verb + て form is used to connect a verb to another verb, or another part of the sentence. It's commonly used to list actions in sequence, such as 食べて寝る ('I eat, and (then) sleep'). Adding から after the て form emphasizes the sequence, as in 食べてから寝る ('I eat, and (after that) I will sleep').\n上で\nうえで\nAfter, Upon\nN3 Grammar\nてから and 上で both convey a sequence of events, but their nuances differ. てから simply indicates that one event follows another. In contrast, 上で emphasizes that the first action or event was a necessary precondition for the second event. Also, 上で is more formal than てから, and often used in business situations or writing.\nあとで\nあとで\nAfter, Later\nN4 Grammar\nてから and あとで both convey a sequence of events, but their nuances differ. てから uses the Verb + て form to show that one event follows another. In contrast, あとで follows the past tense (た form) and simply indicates that the second event occurred after the first, without implying any connection between the two.\nたら\nWhen, From when, Just when, If\nN4 Grammar\nてから and たら both convey a sequence of events, but their nuances differ. てから simply indicates that one event follows another. In contrast, たら is similar to the English 'when' or 'if' and suggests that the second event is a result of the first. たら can be used in both hypothetical situations ('if A, then B') and past events ('When I did A, B happened').\nVocab Coverage\nAll Bunpro Vocab that appears on this item.\nExpand List\nKnowledge Check\nExamples\n--:--\nSentence\nTranslation\n日本語\n(\nにほんご\n)\nの\n勉強\n(\nべんきょう\n)\nを\nしてから\n、\n日本\n(\nにほん\n)\nに\n行\n(\nい\n)\nきます\n。\nOnce I study\nJapanese, I will go to Japan.\n日本\n(\nにほん\n)\nに\n行\n(\nい\n)\nってから\n、\n日本語\n(\nにほんご\n)\nの\n勉強\n(\nべんきょう\n)\nを\nします\n。\nAfter going\nto Japan, I will study Japanese.\nこの\n本\n(\nほん\n)\nを\n読\n(\nよ\n)\nんでから\n、\n返\n(\nかえ\n)\nす\n。\nOnce I've read\nthis book, I will return it.\n暇\n(\nひま\n)\nに\nなってから\n、ゆっくり\n旅行\n(\nりょこう\n)\nに\n行\n(\nい\n)\nき\nたい\n。\nAfter becoming\nfree, I want to take a nice, long trip.\n雪\n(\nゆき\n)\nが\n降\n(\nふ\n)\nってから\n、スキーに\n行\n(\nい\n)\nく\n。\nOnce it snows\n, I will go skiing.\nGet more example sentences!\nPremium users get access to 12 example sentences on all Grammar Points.\nTry Bunpro\nSelf-Study Sentences\nStudy your own way!\nAdd sentences and study them alongside Bunpro sentences.\nTry Bunpro\nOnline\n「てから」\nGuidetoLearnJapanese\nBrief note of て-form with 「から」\nTae Kim\nてから vs. たら\nHiNative\nOffline\n[DBJG] A Dictionary of Basic Japanese Grammar\nPage 177\nGenki II 1st Edition\nPage 101\nGenki II 2nd Edition\nPage 127\nGenki II 3rd Edition\nPage 123\nMarugoto Elementary 2 (A2) Rikai\nPage 49\nみんなの日本語 I\nPage 104 [CH 16]\nTrack Resources!\nBunpro tracks all of the resources you’ve visited, and offers relevant bookmarks of physical books to help with offline tracking.\nTry Bunpro\nてから – Grammar Discussion\nMost Recent Replies (17 in total)\nAlex7s\nThanks\nLemonadeXG\n暇になってから、ゆっくり旅行に行きたい。\nCan someone explain why the “な” is present in this sentence?\nEdit: Apologies, I completely forgot the ‘become’ part of this knowledge check.\nIcyIceBear\nWelcome to the community anyhow\nGot questions about てから?\nJoin us to discuss, ask, and learn together!\nJoin the Discussion\nBunpro\nSimplifying Japanese\nOfficial Apps\nLearn More\nJoin us!\nCompany\nNews\nCareers\nAbout Us\nTestimonials\nAcknowledgements\nFor Teachers\nJapanese\nOfficial Forums\nContent Search\nReading Practice\nGrammar Library\nHiragana & Katakana\nSupport\nContact Us\nSupport & FAQ\n© 2026, Bunpro SRS.\nRead our\nTerms of Service\n,\nPrivacy Policy\nand\nCompany Overview\n.\nMade with\n❤️\nfrom Osaka.\nEnglish",
