      "sourceText": "まだ～ていません (JLPT N5) | Bunpro\nLoading user data...\nBunpro\nGrammar Info\nN5 Lesson 7: 10/13\nまだ～ていません\nStill haven't done (something)\nDetails\nExamples\nResources\nまだ～ていません\nStill haven't done (something)\nDetails\nExamples\nResources\nDetails\nExamples\nResources\nReady to transform your studies?\nLearn N5 in under a month!\nTry now, no credit card required!\nTry Bunpro\nLearn More\nStructure\nStandard\nPolite\nまだ\n+\nVerb［て］+\nいない\nDetails\nPart of Speech\nExpression\nWord Type\nAuxiliary Verb\nRegister\nStandard\nRare Kanji\n未だ\nAbout まだ～ていません\nまだ～ていません\nis a regular expression that combines the\nadverb\nまだ, with the\nconjunction particle\nて\n. The\nて\nform will be followed by the verb\nいる\nin its negative\nいません\n(polite), or\nいない\n(casual) form. This expression has the meaning of 'to still not have done (A)'.\nFrom these examples, it can be seen that this grammatical structure follows the regular rules of conjugation for the\nて\nform.\nTopics\nStill? Enough Already!\nN5 Topic\nIn this Topic, we're going to learn how to say that something 'already is' and 'still is'. To do this, we will use the adverbs もう and まだ. For this pair of words, special attention needs to be paid to how tense and ている interact with them to create natural sentences.\n3m\nRelated\nExpand All\nまだ\nStill\nN5 Grammar\nまだ suggests that something remains in a state, or that an action has not yet occurred, similar to the English 'still' or 'not yet.' When used with a verb in the ていません form, it expresses the continued non-occurrence of an action. For example, まだ食べていません means 'I haven't eaten yet' or 'I still haven't eaten.'\nVerb[volitional]とする\nう・よう + とする\nTry to, Attempt to, To be about to\nN3 Grammar\nThe grammar point 'Verb[volitional]とする' expresses the speaker's decision or intention to do something, often indicating a plan or goal. In contrast, 'まだ～ていません' is used to express that an action has not yet occurred or a state has not yet been reached, emphasizing the ongoing absence of the action or state.\nVocab Coverage\nAll Bunpro Vocab that appears on this item.\nExpand List\nKnowledge Check\nExamples\n--:--\nSentence\nTranslation\nまだ\n食\n(\nた\n)\nべていません\n。\nI\nstill\nhaven't eaten\n.\nその\n本\n(\nほん\n)\nを\nまだ\n読\n(\nよ\n)\nんでいません\n。\nI\nstill\nhaven't read\nthat book.\nまだ\n勉強\n(\nべんきょう\n)\nしていません\n。\nI\nstill\nhaven't studied\n.\nこの\n漢字\n(\nかんじ\n)\nを\nまだ\n習\n(\nなら\n)\nっていません\n。\nI\nstill\nhaven't learned\nthis kanji.\n学校\n(\nがっこう\n)\nに\nまだ\n行\n(\nい\n)\nっていません\n。\nI\nstill\nhaven't gone\nto school.\nGet more example sentences!\nPremium users get access to 12 example sentences on all Grammar Points.\nTry Bunpro\nSelf-Study Sentences\nStudy your own way!\nAdd sentences and study them alongside Bunpro sentences.\nTry Bunpro\nOnline\nHaven't done yet\nJapanese Ammo\nまだ～ていません\nE-Japanese\nOffline\nGenki I\nPage 176\nGenki I 2nd Edition\nPage 214\nGenki I 3rd Edition\nPage 217\nみんなの日本語 II\nPage 42 [CH 31]\nTrack Resources!\nBunpro tracks all of the resources you’ve visited, and offers relevant bookmarks of physical books to help with offline tracking.\nTry Bunpro\nまだ～ていません – Grammar Discussion\nMost Recent Replies (12 in total)\nka5\nFor that, you have to reference a small footnote in ている② (JLPT N5) | Bunpro, い in ～ている can be omitted (and ～ていない is just a negative ～ている).\nepi123\nOof you made me realise I skipped the yellow text how stupid of me! Thank you for taking the time to reply!\nNow it all makes sense, thanks again : D\ndarzington\nWhat would it mean to negate the verb instead of ている, if anything?\nLike まだ読まなくています ?\nWhen asked for this grammar point I get mixed up about where the negation is meant to occur, and somehow this makes more sense to me. I’d think that ていません means something more like “not in the state of…”\nGot questions about まだ～ていません?\nJoin us to discuss, ask, and learn together!\nJoin the Discussion\nBunpro\nSimplifying Japanese\nOfficial Apps\nLearn More\nJoin us!\nCompany\nNews\nCareers\nAbout Us\nTestimonials\nAcknowledgements\nFor Teachers\nJapanese\nOfficial Forums\nContent Search\nReading Practice\nGrammar Library\nHiragana & Katakana\nSupport\nContact Us\nSupport & FAQ\n© 2026, Bunpro SRS.\nRead our\nTerms of Service\n,\nPrivacy Policy\nand\nCompany Overview\n.\nMade with\n❤️\nfrom Osaka.\nEnglish",
