      "sourceText": "どうして (JLPT N5) | Bunpro\nLoading user data...\nBunpro\nGrammar Info\nN5 Lesson 6: 3/17\nどうして\nWhy\nDetails\nExamples\nResources\nどうして\nWhy\nDetails\nExamples\nResources\nDetails\nExamples\nResources\nReady to transform your studies?\nLearn N5 in under a month!\nTry now, no credit card required!\nTry Bunpro\nLearn More\nStructure\nどうして\n+ Question\nDetails\nPart of Speech\nAdverb\nWord Type\nIndependent Word\nRegister\nStandard\nAbout どうして\nどうして is a polite and versatile way to ask 'why' in Japanese. It can carry a feeling of wanting to know the process or story behind something, literally coming from どう 'how' and して (the て form of する, 'to do'). It is like asking 'how did it come to be that (A)?', and can sometimes express curiosity or surprise.\nOf the three common ways to say 'why' in Japanese, どうして is the most neutral, with なぜ being more formal and なんで being more casual.\nCaution\nBe careful not to confuse どうして with the similar sounding phrase どうした. While どうして asks 'why?', どうした is used to show concern and ask 'what's wrong?' or 'what happened?'. どうした will often be followed by の, and the polite form どうしましたか may also be seen.\nTopics\nWho? And Why, Why, Why?\nN5 Topic\nIn this Topic, we're going to learn about question words and also look at Japanese question patterns in more detail, combining a variety of grammar points we already know.\n4m\nSynonyms\nExpand All\nなぜ\nWhy\nN5 Grammar\nBoth なぜ and どうして are relatively polite question words that can seek a reason, similar to the English 'why'. Of the two, なぜ is more formal, logical, and typical of the written language, while どうして is the most neutral 'why' in Japanese, is used in writing and speaking, and can express more emotion than なぜ.\nなんで\nWhy\nN5 Grammar\nBoth どうして and なんで are question words that seek a reason, like the English 'why'. Of the two, どうして is more polite and neutral, and can be used in written or spoken language in a wide variety of situations. なんで is more casual/colloquial, and most often used in informal conversation with close friends (and should be avoided with superiors like teachers/bosses, as it can sound demanding in those cases).\nVocab Coverage\nAll Bunpro Vocab that appears on this item.\nExpand List\nKnowledge Check\nExamples\n--:--\nSentence\nTranslation\nどうして\nここにいるの？\nWhy\nare you here?\nどうして\nこれを\n食\n(\nた\n)\nべたの？\nWhy\ndid you eat this?\nどうして\n夢\n(\nゆめ\n)\nを\n見\n(\nみ\n)\nるの？\nWhy\ndo we dream?\nどうして\n泣\n(\nな\n)\nいているの？\nWhy\nare you crying?\nいつもここに\n置\n(\nお\n)\nくのは\nどうして\n？\nWhy\ndo you always put it here?\nGet more example sentences!\nPremium users get access to 12 example sentences on all Grammar Points.\nTry Bunpro\nSelf-Study Sentences\nStudy your own way!\nAdd sentences and study them alongside Bunpro sentences.\nTry Bunpro\nOnline\nThere are no Online resources listed for 「どうして」.\nYou can\nsubmit a resource for review\n. Resources are constantly updated, come back later to see new additions!\nOffline\nThere are no Offline resources listed for 「どうして」.\nYou can\nsubmit a resource for review\n. Resources are constantly updated, come back later to see new additions!\nTrack Resources!\nBunpro tracks all of the resources you’ve visited, and offers relevant bookmarks of physical books to help with offline tracking.\nTry Bunpro\nどうして – Grammar Discussion\nThere's currently no discussion for どうして\nAsk questions and learn together with other Bunpro users!\nJoin the Discussion\nBunpro\nSimplifying Japanese\nOfficial Apps\nLearn More\nJoin us!\nCompany\nNews\nCareers\nAbout Us\nTestimonials\nAcknowledgements\nFor Teachers\nJapanese\nOfficial Forums\nContent Search\nReading Practice\nGrammar Library\nHiragana & Katakana\nSupport\nContact Us\nSupport & FAQ\n© 2026, Bunpro SRS.\nRead our\nTerms of Service\n,\nPrivacy Policy\nand\nCompany Overview\n.\nMade with\n❤️\nfrom Osaka.\nEnglish",
