      "sourceText": "だった・でした (JLPT N5) | Bunpro\nLoading user data...\nBunpro\nGrammar Info\nN5 Lesson 6: 7/17\nだった・でした\nWas, Were (Past tense)\nい-Adjectives cannot be used with だった・でした\nDetails\nExamples\nResources\nだった・でした\nWas, Were (Past tense)\nDetails\nExamples\nResources\nDetails\nExamples\nResources\nReady to transform your studies?\nLearn N5 in under a month!\nTry now, no credit card required!\nTry Bunpro\nLearn More\nStructure\nStandard\nPolite\nNoun +\nだった\n［な］Adjective\n+\nだった\nDetails\nPart of Speech\nAuxiliary Verb\nRegister\nStandard\nAbout だった・でした\nIn order to say that something 'was' a certain way in Japanese, you will need to use\nだった\n(casual) or\nでした\n(polite) attached to the end of a noun or\nな-Adjective\n. This is simply a combination of two\nauxiliary verbs\n,\nだ\n(or\nです\nwhen polite) with た. For\nだった\n, we will need to add った to the base form of\nだ\n. For\nです\n, す will change to し before adding た.\nCaution\nThe past form of\nい-Adjectives\ncannot be linked with\nだった\nor\nでした\n, as they have their own set of conjugation rules.\nPractice だった・でした in\nKaijugation\nThe only conjugation game with collateral damage!\nPlay!\nTopics\nIt Was the Best of Times\nN5 Topic\nIn this Topic, we're going to learn how to talk about nouns and な-Adjectives in the past tense. As usual, this is different for polite and standard language. With this we will be able to use all applicable word types in the past tense (い-Adjectives, verbs, な-Adjectives, and nouns)!\n2m\nRelated\nExpand All\nう-Verb (Past)\nう - Verbs (Past tense)\nN5 Grammar\nThe past form of う-Verbs expresses a completed action or an event that took place in the past, similar to the English '-ed.' In contrast, だった and でした are used after nouns to express the past tense, indicating that something 'was' or 'were' in a certain state. While the meaning (something happened or existed in the past) is the same, the grammatical expression differs depending on the word type (verb vs. noun).\nだ\nTo be, Is\nN5 Grammar\nだった・でした and だ are all used to assert or identify something. The difference among them is in formality and tense. だ is casual and present tense (similar to the English 'is'/'am'), while だった・でした is past tense ('was'), with だった being casual (the past tense of だ) and でした being polite (the past tense of です).\nです\nTo be, Is\nN5 Grammar\nです and だった・でした are all forms of 'is' or 'to be,' but they show different tenses. です is used for the present or future, like in あれは猫です ('That is a cat'). だった and でした are past tense—だった is casual, and でした is polite. For example, あれは猫だった means 'That was a cat.'\nVocab Coverage\nAll Bunpro Vocab that appears on this item.\nExpand List\nKnowledge Check\nExamples\n--:--\nSentence\nTranslation\n綺麗\n(\nきれい\n)\nだった\n。\nIt\nwas\nbeautiful.\nトム\nだった\n。\nIt\nwas\nTom.\nそれ\nは\n、\n昨日\n(\nきのう\n)\nでした\n。\nThat\nwas\nyesterday.\n猫\n(\nねこ\n)\nが\n大\n(\nだい\n)\n好\n(\nす\n)\nき\nだった\n。\nI really lik\ned\ncats. (Cats\nwere\nlov\ned\nby me)\n大変\n(\nたいへん\n)\nだった\n。\nIt\nwas\nterrible.\nGet more example sentences!\nPremium users get access to 12 example sentences on all Grammar Points.\nTry Bunpro\nSelf-Study Sentences\nStudy your own way!\nAdd sentences and study them alongside Bunpro sentences.\nTry Bunpro\nOnline\nAdjectives Past & Past Negatives\nJapanese Ammo\nConjugating to the past state-of-being\nTae Kim\nUnder Nouns and Adjectives\nFluentu\nOffline\nGenki I 3rd Edition\nPage 214\nTae Kim's Japanese Grammar Guide\nPage 32\nみんなの日本語 I\nPage 128 [CH 20]\nTrack Resources!\nBunpro tracks all of the resources you’ve visited, and offers relevant bookmarks of physical books to help with offline tracking.\nTry Bunpro\nだった・でした – Grammar Discussion\nThere's currently no discussion for だった・でした\nAsk questions and learn together with other Bunpro users!\nJoin the Discussion\nBunpro\nSimplifying Japanese\nOfficial Apps\nLearn More\nJoin us!\nCompany\nNews\nCareers\nAbout Us\nTestimonials\nAcknowledgements\nFor Teachers\nJapanese\nOfficial Forums\nContent Search\nReading Practice\nGrammar Library\nHiragana & Katakana\nSupport\nContact Us\nSupport & FAQ\n© 2026, Bunpro SRS.\nRead our\nTerms of Service\n,\nPrivacy Policy\nand\nCompany Overview\n.\nMade with\n❤️\nfrom Osaka.\nEnglish",
