      "sourceText": "い-Adjectives くない (JLPT N5) | Bunpro\nLoading user data...\nBunpro\nGrammar Info\nN5 Lesson 4: 13/13\nくない\nNot (Adjective)\nい-Adjectives, whether positive or negative, cannot be used with だ\nDetails\nExamples\nResources\nい-Adjectives くない\nNot (Adjective)\nDetails\nExamples\nResources\nDetails\nExamples\nResources\nReady to transform your studies?\nLearn N5 in under a month!\nTry now, no credit card required!\nTry Bunpro\nLearn More\nStructure\nStandard\nPolite\n［い］Adjective［く］\n+\nない\nExamples:\nおもしろ\nく\n+\nない\n新\n(\nあたら\n)\nし\nく\n+\nない\nDetails\nPart of Speech\nAdjective\nWord Type\nAuxiliary Verb\nRegister\nStandard\nAbout い-Adjectives くない\nThe negative form of\nい-Adjectives\nin Japanese is created by using the\nconjunctive form\nof the adjective, followed by\nない\n.\nConjunctive form\njust means 'agglutinative', or 'conjunctive' in Japanese. For\nい-Adjectives\n, this\nconjunctive form\nis created by removing い, and replacing it with く.\nThe\nない\nused with\nい-Adjectives\nis considered to be a different word to the\nない\nused with verbs. When used with\nい-Adjectives\n,\nない\nitself is also an\nい-Adjective\n. This means that it follows the same rules as regular\nい-Adjectives\n. Due to ません (the polite negative form) being an\nauxiliary verb\n,  it cannot be conjugated with\nい-Adjectives\nin the same way as verbs.\nAs can be seen here, you must first add the verb\nある\n, and then conjugate it into its negative form using the\nauxiliary verb\nません. This is how the polite negative is created.\nCaution\nAs with regular\nい-Adjectives\n, you cannot use\nだ\nafter\nない\n.\nです\nis acceptable to create a semi-polite form, but is best used in spoken language only.\nPractice くない in\nKaijugation\nThe only conjugation game with collateral damage!\nPlay!\nTopics\nThat's Not So Bad\nN5 Topic\nIn this Topic, we're going to learn about the negative form of い-Adjectives. With this, we'll be able to say that something is ‘not’ delicious, ‘not’ amazing, or ‘not’ cute!\n1m\nRelated\nExpand All\nじゃない\nIs not, Isn't\nN5 Grammar\nい-Adjectives form a negative by replacing い with くない (e.g., 赤い = 'it's red,' 赤くない = 'it's not red'). For nouns and な-Adjectives, the negative is formed by adding じゃない (e.g., 大変じゃない = 'it's not difficult,' バナナじゃない = 'it's not a banana'). Both forms are plain and used in casual conversation or other grammatical patterns.\nVocab Coverage\nAll Bunpro Vocab that appears on this item.\nExpand List\nKnowledge Check\nExamples\n--:--\nSentence\nTranslation\n暑\n(\nあつ\n)\nくないです\n。\nIt is\nnot hot\n.\n今日\n(\nきょう\n)\nは\n寒\n(\nさむ\n)\nくない\n。\nIt is\nnot cold\ntoday.\nこれ\nは\n楽\n(\nたの\n)\nしくない\nです\n。\nThis is\nnot fun\n.\n新\n(\nあたら\n)\nしくない\nコンピューター。\nA computer that is\nnot new\n.\nそれ\nは\n安\n(\nやす\n)\nくないです\n。\nThat is\nnot cheap\n.\nGet more example sentences!\nPremium users get access to 12 example sentences on all Grammar Points.\nTry Bunpro\nSelf-Study Sentences\nStudy your own way!\nAdd sentences and study them alongside Bunpro sentences.\nTry Bunpro\nOnline\nAdjectives\nGuideToJapanese\nAdjectives\nImabi\nい Adjective negative form\nTofugu\nOffline\nGenki 1\nPage 132\nGenki I 3rd Edition\nPage 133\nTrack Resources!\nBunpro tracks all of the resources you’ve visited, and offers relevant bookmarks of physical books to help with offline tracking.\nTry Bunpro\nい-Adjectives くない – Grammar Discussion\nMost Recent Replies (6 in total)\nRuslan_Montana\nゲームは難しくありません。\nvs\nゲームは難しくない(です）\nWhat is the difference?\nKlariss\nhi, there is no big difference here. It’s basically the same whether you use the first or second example. To me, the first example sounds more formal.\nI hope I’m not wrong, if so, someone please correct me.\nSamihh\nYou’re right, furthermore in few circonstances and when you’re writting, you should choose ありません.\nGot questions about い-Adjectives くない?\nJoin us to discuss, ask, and learn together!\nJoin the Discussion\nBunpro\nSimplifying Japanese\nOfficial Apps\nLearn More\nJoin us!\nCompany\nNews\nCareers\nAbout Us\n