      "sourceText": "誰 (JLPT N5) | Bunpro\nLoading user data...\nBunpro\nGrammar Info\nN5 Lesson 6: 1/17\n誰\n(\nだれ\n)\nWho\nDetails\nExamples\nResources\n誰\nWho\nDetails\nExamples\nResources\nDetails\nExamples\nResources\nReady to transform your studies?\nLearn N5 in under a month!\nTry now, no credit card required!\nTry Bunpro\nLearn More\nStructure\nだれ\nDetails\nPart of Speech\nNoun\nWord Type\nPronoun\nRegister\nStandard\nAbout 誰\n誰\n(\nだれ\n)\nis a\nsubstitute noun\nthat is used in Japanese to describe unknown people. Due to Japanese particles behaving in very specific ways,\n誰\n(\nだれ\n)\nwill be translated differently depending on the particle that follows it.\n誰\n(\nだれ\n)\nが\n・\n誰\n(\nだれ\n)\nで\n・\n誰\n(\nだれ\n)\nに\n・\n誰\n(\nだれ\n)\nを\n(who),\n誰\n(\nだれ\n)\nの\n(whose),\n誰\n(\nだれ\n)\nか\n(somebody),\n誰\n(\nだれ\n)\nも\n(any/everybody).\nCaution\nDepending on the style of polite speech, there are several different words that will be used to indicate an unknown person. どなた is used in\nhonorific language\n, while どちらさま is used in\npolite speech\n.\nTopics\nWho? And Why, Why, Why?\nN5 Topic\nIn this Topic, we're going to learn about question words and also look at Japanese question patterns in more detail, combining a variety of grammar points we already know.\n4m\nRelated\nExpand All\n誰か・どこか・誰も・どこも\nだれか・どこか・だれも・どこも\nSomeone, Somewhere, Not anyone, Not anywhere\nN5 Grammar\n誰 is a noun that refers to an unknown person, similar to the English 'who.' A common use is to ask about someone's identity, as in あの人は誰ですか ('Who is that person?') 誰 can also combine with other particles to express concepts like 誰か ('somebody'), 誰の ('whose'), and 誰も ('everyone' or 'no one' when used with a negative).\nVocab Coverage\nAll Bunpro Vocab that appears on this item.\nExpand List\nKnowledge Check\nExamples\n--:--\nSentence\nTranslation\n誰\n(\nだれ\n)\nです\nか\n。\nWho\nis it?\n誰\n(\nだれ\n)\nがいます\nか\n。\nWho\nis there?\n誰\n(\nだれ\n)\nが\nします\nか\n。\nWho\nwill do it?\nこれ\nは\n誰\n(\nだれ\n)\nの\nパソコン\nです\nか\n。\nWhose\ncomputer is this?\n彼\n(\nかれ\n)\nは\n誰\n(\nだれ\n)\nでしょう\n。\nI wonder\nwho\nhe is.\nGet more example sentences!\nPremium users get access to 12 example sentences on all Grammar Points.\nTry Bunpro\nSelf-Study Sentences\nStudy your own way!\nAdd sentences and study them alongside Bunpro sentences.\nTry Bunpro\nOnline\nJapanese wh-Questions\nWasabi\nだれ\nJapanese for Beginners\nOffline\n[DBJG] A Dictionary of Basic Japanese Grammar\nPage 13\nGenki I 2nd Edition\nPage 64\nGenki I 3rd Edition\nPage 62\nTrack Resources!\nBunpro tracks all of the resources you’ve visited, and offers relevant bookmarks of physical books to help with offline tracking.\nTry Bunpro\n誰 – Grammar Discussion\nMost Recent Replies (6 in total)\njunetheway\nHello, everyone!\nI have a simple question.\nお前は誰で行く？\nThis phrase is in the examples, but I think 誰と is more natural than 誰で.\nWhat do you think?\nDo people use 誰で frequently?\nFuga\nHey @junetheway !\nBoth 誰で and 誰と would work here! However, changing で to と would change the nuance of the sentence completely.\nThis sentence uses this で, which is used to highlight something/someone that is required to perform an action. This means that this で gives this sentence the nuance of ‘Who are you choosing’ instead of ‘going together’. A sentence like this may be heard when playing a video game that requires each players to pick a character.\nHope this clears it up!\njunetheway\nOh, I see!!\nThe video game example really made me understand the difference!!\nThank you so much for the explanation!!\nGot questions about 誰?\nJoin us to discuss, ask, and learn together!\nJoin the Discussion\nBunpro\nSimplifying Japanese\nOfficial Apps\nLearn More\nJoin us!\nCompany\nNews\nCareers\nAbout Us\nTestimonials\nAcknowledgements\nFor Teachers\nJapanese\nOfficial Forums\nContent Search\nReading Practice\nGrammar Library\nHiragana & Katakana\nSupport\nContact Us\nSupport & FAQ\n© 2026, Bunpro SRS.\nRead our\nTerms of Service\n,\nPrivacy Policy\nand\nCompany Overview\