      "sourceText": "なぜ (JLPT N5) | Bunpro\nLoading user data...\nBunpro\nGrammar Info\nN5 Lesson 6: 2/17\nなぜ\nWhy\nDetails\nExamples\nResources\nなぜ\nWhy\nDetails\nExamples\nResources\nDetails\nExamples\nResources\nReady to transform your studies?\nLearn N5 in under a month!\nTry now, no credit card required!\nTry Bunpro\nLearn More\nStructure\nなぜ\n+ Question\nDetails\nPart of Speech\nAdverb\nWord Type\nIndependent Word\nRegister\nStandard\nAbout なぜ\nなぜ is the formal way to ask 'why' in Japanese. It is often seen in writing, formal speeches, or in serious situations when asking for a logical reason or cause for something. As it is direct and formal, it can sound slightly stiff in everyday casual conversation.\nOf the three common ways to say 'why' in Japanese, なぜ is the most formal, followed by\nどうして\n, with\nなんで\nbeing the most casual.\nFun Fact\nAlthough slightly rarer, なぜ may also be seen in its kanji form\n何故\n(\nなぜ\n)\n, literally meaning 'what cause'. As with a lot of words which are normally written in kana but may sometimes be written in kanji,\n何故\n(\nなぜ\n)\nwill more typically be seen in more formal or literary writing.\nTopics\nWho? And Why, Why, Why?\nN5 Topic\nIn this Topic, we're going to learn about question words and also look at Japanese question patterns in more detail, combining a variety of grammar points we already know.\n4m\nSynonyms\nExpand All\nなんで\nWhy\nN5 Grammar\nBoth なぜ and なんで are question words that seek a reason, similar to the English 'why'. They differ in that なぜ tends to be more formal, logical, and written-style, while なんで is more colloquial, emotive, and typical of spoken language.\nどうして\nWhy\nN5 Grammar\nBoth なぜ and どうして are relatively polite question words that can seek a reason, similar to the English 'why'. Of the two, なぜ is more formal, logical, and typical of the written language, while どうして is the most neutral 'why' in Japanese, is used in writing and speaking, and can express more emotion than なぜ.\nVocab Coverage\nAll Bunpro Vocab that appears on this item.\nExpand List\nKnowledge Check\nExamples\n--:--\nSentence\nTranslation\nなぜ\n雪\n(\nゆき\n)\nは\n白\n(\nしろ\n)\nいの？\nWhy\nis snow white?\nなぜ\nあの\n海\n(\nうみ\n)\nは\n汚\n(\nきたな\n)\nい？\nWhy\nis that sea dirty?\nなぜ\nここに\n猫\n(\nねこ\n)\nがいるの？\nWhy\nis there a cat here?\nなぜ\n水\n(\nみず\n)\nを\n買\n(\nか\n)\nったんですか？\nWhy\ndid you buy water?\nなぜ\n、\n彼\n(\nかれ\n)\nは\n面白\n(\nおもしろ\n)\nいの？\nWhy\nis he funny?\nGet more example sentences!\nPremium users get access to 12 example sentences on all Grammar Points.\nTry Bunpro\nSelf-Study Sentences\nStudy your own way!\nAdd sentences and study them alongside Bunpro sentences.\nTry Bunpro\nOnline\nThere are no Online resources listed for 「なぜ」.\nYou can\nsubmit a resource for review\n. Resources are constantly updated, come back later to see new additions!\nOffline\nThere are no Offline resources listed for 「なぜ」.\nYou can\nsubmit a resource for review\n. Resources are constantly updated, come back later to see new additions!\nTrack Resources!\nBunpro tracks all of the resources you’ve visited, and offers relevant bookmarks of physical books to help with offline tracking.\nTry Bunpro\nなぜ – Grammar Discussion\nMost Recent Replies (4 in total)\nThe111\nWhy is this a hard failure?\nFuga\nHey @The111 !\nThis works here, so I have added it to the list of answers we accept! Thank you for letting us know about this!\nThe111\nThank you!\nGot questions about なぜ?\nJoin us to discuss, ask, and learn together!\nJoin the Discussion\nBunpro\nSimplifying Japanese\nOfficial Apps\nLearn More\nJoin us!\nCompany\nNews\nCareers\nAbout Us\nTestimonials\nAcknowledgements\nFor Teachers\nJapanese\nOfficial Forums\nContent Search\nReading Practice\nGrammar Library\nHiragana & Katakana\nSupport\nContact Us\nSupport & FAQ\n© 2026, Bunpro SRS.\nRead our\nTerms of Service\n,\nPrivacy Policy\nand\nCompany Overview\n.\nMade with\n❤️\nfrom Osaka.\nEnglish",
