      "sourceText": "Adjective + て・Noun + で (JLPT N5) | Bunpro\nLoading user data...\nBunpro\nGrammar Info\nN5 Lesson 10: 3/12\n～て (Adjectives and Nouns)\nAnd... (Conjunctive)\nDetails\nExamples\nResources\nAdjective + て・Noun +...\nAnd... (Conjunctive)\nDetails\nExamples\nResources\nDetails\nExamples\nResources\nReady to transform your studies?\nLearn N5 in under a month!\nTry now, no credit card required!\nTry Bunpro\nLearn More\nStructure\n［い］Adjective［\nい\n］\n+\nく\n+\nて\nおもしろ\nい\n+\nく\n+\nて\n新\n(\nあたら\n)\nし\nい\n+\nく\n+\nて\n［な］Adjective\n+\nで\nしずか +\nで\n好\n(\nす\n)\nき +\nで\nNoun +\nで\n先生\n(\nせんせい\n)\n+\nで\n仕事\n(\nしごと\n)\n+\nで\nExceptions:\nいい\n→\nよく\nて\nDetails\nPart of Speech\nAdjective + Conjunctions\nWord Type\nParticle / Auxiliary Verb\nRegister\nStandard\nAbout Adjective + て・Noun + で\nThe\nて\nform of an\nい-Adjective\n, or\nで\nform of a noun (or\nな-Adjective\n) is exactly the same as the\nて\nform of a verb, in that it carries the meaning of 'and', and is used for linking. It will allow us to list multiple qualities/traits of something.\nFor\nい-Adjectives\n, we will need to change the last い to く (the form used for conjugation), and then simply add\nて\n.\nFor nouns and\nな-Adjectives\n, we will need to add\nで\nto the base form (not\nな\nor\nだ\n).\nIt should be noted that\nて\nand\nで\nare different structures here.\nて\nis the same conjunction particle that is used with verbs (meaning that\nい-Adjectives\nare similar to verbs), while\nで\nis actually a form of\nだ\nthat is used for conjugation. It is the same\nで\nas the one that is used in the formal version of\nだ\n,\nである\n. Which we will learn later.\nCaution\nLike other\nて\nforms (\nている 1\n,\nている 2\n, and\nている 3\n), the\nて\n(or\nで\n) form of other words can have several possible meanings. These meanings are as follows.\nLinking - Like 'and' in English.\nReasons - Like 'with (A)', or 'because of (A)' in English.\nManner - Like 'to do (B) in an (A) way' in English.\nCaution\nAs with all other conjugations of\nいい\n, remember that it will be よくて, and not いくて.\nTopics\nTe-rrific て-Form\nN5 Topic\nIn this Topic, we're going to learn about how the て-form is used with adjectives and nouns. It is much the same as with verbs, being used to connect two things together. In the details section, we will also recap the logic and use of the て-form in general.\n2m\nRelated\nExpand All\nVerb + て+ B\n～て (Sequence)\nAnd, And then, After that (sequence)\nN5 Grammar\nAdjective + て, Noun + で, and Verb + て+ B are the same fundamental pattern, using the て form to connect elements in a sentence. The construction of the て form depends on whether the word is an い-Adjective, な-Adjective, noun, or verb, but the function remains consistent, similar to the English 'and.'\nAdjective + て + B\n～て (Qualities and States)\nAnd..., Both and (Conjunctive)\nN5 Grammar\nBoth of these patterns involve connecting an adjective or noun phrase to the rest of the sentence using the て form. The meaning of the connection depends on context. Sometimes it simply links words, as in 大きくてきれい ('big and pretty'), while in other cases, the first part may provide a reason for the second, as in 甘くておいしい ('sweet and tasty').\nなくて\nなくて (Sequence)\nTo not ~ and ~, Not ~ and ~ (Conjugations)\nN4 Grammar\nAdjective + て or Noun + で is used to connect adjective or noun phrases with the rest of the sentence, similar to the English 'and.' なくて is similar, but connects phrases that are in the negative (ない) form. For example, 安くてよかった means 'I'm glad it was inexpensive,' while 高くなくてよかった would mean 'I'm glad that it wasn't expensive'.\nVerb[て] + B\n～て (Reasons and Causes)\nAnd・and so, Due to, Because of, Since, Conjunctive\nN4 Grammar\nBoth of these patterns involve connecting a word or phrase (adjectives and nouns in one case, verbs in the other) to the rest of the sentence using the て form. The meaning of the connection depends on context. Sometimes it simply links words, as in 大きくてきれい ('big and pretty'), while in other cases, the て form expresses reason or method, as in 歩いて行った ('went by walking').\n連用形\nれんようけい\nFormal Conjunctive\nN3 Grammar\n連用形 also replaces て or で after adjectives and nouns in formal writing. For example, 優しくて becomes 優しく, e.g. とても優しくて、綺麗です 'She's very kind, and pretty.' → とても優しく、綺麗です. (Same meaning, but more formal and literary.)\nVocab Coverage\nAll Bunpro Vocab that appears on this item.\nExpand List\nKnowledge Check\nExamples\n--:--\nSentence\nTranslation\n新\n(\nあたら\n)\nし\nい\n→\n新\n(\nあたら\n)\nしくて\nNew →\nNew and...\n大\n(\nおお\n)\nき\nい\n→\n大\n(\nおお\n)\nきくて\nBig →\nBig and...\n嫌\n(\nきら\n)\nい\n→\n嫌\n(\nきら\n)\nいで\nDislike →\nDislike and...\n静\n(\nしず\n)\nか →\n静\n(\nしず\n)\nかで\nQuiet →\nQuiet and...\n病気\n(\nびょうき\n)\n→\n病気\n(\nびょうき\n)\nで\nDisease →\nDisease and...\nGet more example sentences!\nPremium users get access to 12 example sentences on all Grammar Points.\nTry Bunpro\nSelf-Study Sentences\nStudy your own way!\nAdd sentences and study them alongside Bunpro sentences.\nTry Bunpro\nOnline\nExpressing a sequence of states\nTae Kim\nて vs. と\nTofugu\nOffline\nTae Kim's Japanese Grammar Guide\nPage 103\nみんなの日本語 I\nPage 104 [CH 16]\nTrack Resources!\nBunpro tracks all of the resources you’ve visited, and offers relevant bookmarks of physical books to help with offline tracking.\nTry Bunpro\nAdjective + て・Noun + で – Grammar Discussion\nMost Recent Replies (13 in total)\nIcyIceBear\nきらい is な adjective so it should be 嫌いで\nIt looks like an い adjective and there’s so way to tell it’s not in this case, it’s one you just have to remember. Don’t worry, it’s one of few\nOldRosy\nThank you!\ncyberjus\nHaving this earlier in the N5 lessons would have reenforced some of the other points. Like ～てもいい\nGot questions about Adjective + て・Noun + で?\nJoin us to discuss, ask, and learn together!\nJoin the Discussion\nBunpro\nSimplifying Japanese\nOfficial Apps\nLearn More\nJoin us!\nCompany\nNews\nCareers\nAbout Us\nTestimonials\nAcknowledgements\nFor Teachers\nJapanese\nOfficial Forums\nContent Search\nReading Practice\nGrammar Library\nHiragana & Katakana\nSupport\nContact Us\nSupport & FAQ\n© 2026, Bunpro SRS.\nRead our\nTerms of Service\n,\nPrivacy Policy\nand\nCompany Overview\n.\nMade with\n❤️\nfrom Osaka.\nEnglish",
