      "sourceText": "どれ (JLPT N5) | Bunpro\nLoading user data...\nBunpro\nGrammar Info\nN5 Lesson 7: 2/13\nどれ\nWhich (of three or more)\nどれ follows a noun, どの precedes a noun\nDetails\nExamples\nResources\nどれ\nWhich (of three or more)\nDetails\nExamples\nResources\nDetails\nExamples\nResources\nReady to transform your studies?\nLearn N5 in under a month!\nTry now, no credit card required!\nTry Bunpro\nLearn More\nStructure\nStandard\nPolite\nNoun + は +\nどれ\nどれ\n+\nが\n(1)\n+ Verb\nどれ\n+\nが\n+\n［い］Adjective\nどれ\n+\nが\n+\n［な］Adjective\n+\nだ\nどれ\n+\nが\n+ Noun +\nだ\n(1)\nを\nDetails\nPart of Speech\nNoun\nWord Type\nPronoun\nRegister\nStandard\nAbout どれ\nどれ\nis from the same family of words as\nこれ\n,\nそれ\n, and\nあれ\n. These words are called こそあど\n言葉\n(\nことば\n)\nin Japanese. Unlike the other 3, which all point to a specific thing, words starting with ど are designed for enquiring about something unknown.\nどれ\ncan roughly be translated as 'which' in English, and is used for enquiring about a group (of 3 or more things).\nFrom these examples, we can see that the particle\nが\nis often used with\nどれ\n, especially when preceding questions. However, when\nどれ\nfollows a noun,\nは\nwill be used.\nWhen there are only two choices to select between,\nどちら\n+\nの\n,  or\nどっち\n+\nの\nwill be used instead of\nどれ\n. This is a habit that has become part of the language over time, and was not originally how these words were used.\nTopics\nWhich? Where? And Which Again?\nN5 Topic\nIn this Topic, we're going to learn about the final piece of the こそあど puzzle. Specifically, words beginning with ど, which are used for identifying unknowns.\n3m\nRelated\nExpand All\nそれ\nThat\nN5 Grammar\nどれ is a question word used to ask 'which' or 'which one' when choosing from three or more options. それ, on the other hand, refers to something near the listener or something already mentioned, similar to 'that' in English. Unlike どれ, それ is not a question word.\nどの\nWhich (of three or more), What (kind)\nN5 Grammar\nどれ and どの are both question words used to ask 'which' when given the option of three or more choices. The key difference is that, while どれ stands alone and asks about one specific thing or choice (i.e. 'Which one,' or 'Which thing'), どの must always be followed by a noun. For example, どの本 means 'Which book'?\nあれ\nThat (over there)\nN5 Grammar\nどれ is a question word used to ask 'which' or 'which one' from a group of three or more options. あれ, on the other hand, refers to something far from both the speaker and listener, or something they both know, similar to 'that' or 'that thing' in English. In short, どれ is used to ask a question, while あれ refers to a specific, distant thing.\nこれ\nThis\nN5 Grammar\nこれ refers to something close to the speaker, like 'this' in English, and can be a physical object or an idea. どれ is a question word that means 'which one?' and is used when choosing from a set of options. In short, これ identifies something specific, while どれ asks about a choice.\nVocab Coverage\nAll Bunpro Vocab that appears on this item.\nExpand List\nKnowledge Check\nExamples\n--:--\nSentence\nTranslation\nどれ\nが\nいい\nです\nか\n。\nWhich\nis good?\nどれ\nでもいい\nです\n。\nWhich\never is fine.\nどれ\nを\n選\n(\nえら\n)\nびます\nか\n。\nWhich\nwill you choose?\nどれ\nが\n好\n(\nす\n)\nき\nです\nか\n。\nWhich\ndo you like?\nどれ\nで\nも\n好\n(\nす\n)\nき\nだ\n。\nI like\nwhich\never。\nGet more example sentences!\nPremium users get access to 12 example sentences on all Grammar Points.\nTry Bunpro\nSelf-Study Sentences\nStudy your own way!\nAdd sentences and study them alongside Bunpro sentences.\nTry Bunpro\nOnline\nJapanese Demonstratives\nWasabi\nWhich: どれ, どちら, どっち, & いずれ\nImabi\nOffline\n[DBJG] A Dictionary of Basic Japanese Grammar\nPage 13\nGenki I 2nd Edition\nPage 62\nGenki I 3rd Edition\nPage 60\nみんなの日本語 I\nPage 105 [CH 16]\nTrack Resources!\nBunpro tracks all of the resources you’ve visited, and offers relevant bookmarks of physical books to help with offline tracking.\nTry Bunpro\nどれ – Grammar Discussion\nThere's currently no discussion for どれ\nAsk questions and learn together with other Bunpro users!\nJoin the Discussion\nBunpro\nSimplifying Japanese\nOfficial Apps\nLearn More\nJoin us!\nCompany\nNews\nCareers\nAbout Us\nTestimonials\nAcknowledgements\nFor Teachers\nJapanese\nOfficial Forums\nContent Search\nReading Practice\nGrammar Library\nHiragana & Katakana\nSupport\nContact Us\nSupport & FAQ\n© 2026, Bunpro SRS.\nRead our\nTerms of Service\n,\nPrivacy Policy\nand\nCompany Overview\n.\nMade with\n❤️\nfrom Osaka.\nEnglish",
