      "sourceText": "たい (JLPT N5) | Bunpro\nLoading user data...\nBunpro\nGrammar Info\nN5 Lesson 7: 12/13\nたい\nWant to do\nThe object of desire can take either the を or が particle\nDetails\nExamples\nResources\nたい\nWant to do\nDetails\nExamples\nResources\nDetails\nExamples\nResources\nReady to transform your studies?\nLearn N5 in under a month!\nTry now, no credit card required!\nTry Bunpro\nLearn More\nStructure\nStandard\nPolite\nVerb［stem］\n+\nた\nい\nVerb［stem］\n+\nた\nくない\nVerb［stem］\n+\nた\nかった\nVerb［stem］\n+\nた\nくなかった\nDetails\nPart of Speech\nAuxiliary Verb\nWord Type\nDependent Word\nRegister\nStandard\nAbout たい\nたい\nis an\nauxiliary verb\nthat is used to express things that you would like to do (want). To use\nたい\n, it needs to be added to the same conjugation base form of a verb that ます would be attached to.\nWhen using\nたい\n, the thing that is 'wanted' can either be marked with\nを\n, or\nが\n. The difference in nuance is that something marked with\nが\nis considered to be wanted more.\nたい\nis conjugated in the same way as\nい-Adjectives\n, meaning that the\nnegative\n,\npast\n, or\npast-negative\nforms may also be used.\nたい\nis only used for expressing things that 'you' want, or repeating information/asking questions about what other people want. It may not be used to make guesses about what other people 'may' want, unless asking them directly.\nCaution\nたい\nis not used to tell other people that you want them to do something. This is done with\n～てほしい\n.\nCaution\nたい\nis not usually used when giving invitations (asking someone if they want to do something with you). In these cases\n～ませんか\nis far more natural.\nPractice たい in\nKaijugation\nThe only conjugation game with collateral damage!\nPlay!\nTopics\nI Want to Do Things Like This and That\nN5 Topic\nIn this Topic, we're going to learn about two unrelated but similar looking pieces of grammar. We're going to learn about たい, which is attached to verbs to say that you 'want to' do them, and たり, which is attached to words to make a generalized list.\n4m\nSynonyms\nExpand All\nたがる\nTo want to (Third person)\nN4 Grammar\nThe たい form expresses personal desires, such as 日本に行きたい ('I want to go to Japan'). がる, on the other hand, is a suffix that shows when someone else appears to want something, like 日本に行きたがっている ('They seem like they want to go to Japan'). The たい form is typically not used for expressing others' desires unless quoting the subject.\nRelated\nExpand All\nそう\nLook like, Appear, Seem, Have a feeling that\nN4 Grammar\nThe たい form expresses personal desires, such as 日本に行きたい ('I want to go to Japan'), though, the たい form is typically not used for expressing others' desires. One way that we can comment on another person's desires, however, is to use the そう form, meaning 'appears to.' For example 日本に行きたそう can be used to mean 'They seem to want to go to Japan.'\nませんか\nWon't you, Would you not, Why don't we\nN5 Grammar\nませんか is a polite way to extend an invitation, similar to 'Wouldn't you like to...?' in English. For example, 何か食べませんか？ ('Won't you eat something?') might be used when politely offering food to a guest. Note that unlike English, the たい form ('Do you want to…?') isn't typically used to invite someone in Japanese—何か食べたいですか？ simply asks if the person wants to eat something.\nてほしい\n～てほしい\nI want you to\nN4 Grammar\nBoth たい and てほしい express a desire, with one key difference. The たい form is used to express your own desires, similar to the English 'I want to...' while てほしい expresses your desires for other people, or in other words, 'I want you to…' For example, 見たい would express your desire to see something, while 見てほしい would be used if you want someone else to take a look.\nがる\nTo feel, To think, To act as if, To want, To desire\nN4 Grammar\nThe たい form expresses personal desires, like バナナが食べたい ('I want to eat a banana'). がる, on the other hand, is used to show that someone else seems to want something, like 食べたがっている ('[He/she] seems like they want to eat'). The たい form is generally not used for others' desires unless the subject has explicitly made their desire clear.\nがほしい\nがほしい\nTo want something, To be in need of\nN4 Grammar\nBoth the たい form and がほしい express desires, similar to the English 'want.' The difference is that たい is used with verbs to express one's desire to perform some action, while がほしい is used after nouns to express one's desire for an object. For example, 日本に行きたい means 'I want to go to Japan' (desire to do something), while お金がほしい means 'I want money' (desire for an object).\nVocab Coverage\nAll Bunpro Vocab that appears on this item.\nExpand List\nKnowledge Check\nExamples\n--:--\nSentence\nTranslation\n日本\n(\nにほん\n)\nに\n行\n(\nい\n)\nきたい\n。\nI want to go\nto Japan.\n来年\n(\nらいねん\n)\n日本\n(\nにほん\n)\nに\n行\n(\nい\n)\nきたい\n。\nNext year,\nI want to go\nto Japan.\n早\n(\nはや\n)\nく\n食\n(\nた\n)\nべたい\n。\nI want to eat\nsoon.\nサッカー\nを\nしたい\nです\n。\nI want to play\nsoccer.\n文法\n(\nぶんぽう\n)\nを\n勉強\n(\nべんきょう\n)\nしたい\nです\n。\nI want to study\ngrammar.\nGet more example sentences!\nPremium users get access to 12 example sentences on all Grammar Points.\nTry Bunpro\nSelf-Study Sentences\nStudy your own way!\nAdd sentences and study them alongside Bunpro sentences.\nTry Bunpro\nOnline\n～たい: Want to do...\nImabi\nAeron Buchanan's Japanese Verb Chart\nWikipedia Commons\nDON'T Want to do\nJapanese Ammo\nVerbs you want to do with 「たい」\nTae Kim\nWant to / たい\nJapanese Ammo\nOffline\n[DBJG] A Dictionary of Basic Japanese Grammar\nPage 1 & 441\nGenki I\nPage 214\nGenki I 2nd Edition\nPage 254\nGenki I 3rd Edition\nPage 258\nMarugoto Elementary 1 (A2) Rikai\nPage 96\nTae Kim's Japanese Grammar Guide\nPage 146\nみんなの日本語 I\nPage 86 [CH 13]\nTrack Resources!\nBunpro tracks all of the resources you’ve visited, and offers relevant bookmarks of physical books to help with offline tracking.\nTry Bunpro\nたい – Grammar Discussion\nMost Recent Replies (15 in total)\nMikkaT\nthanks for the explanation.\njustin.adamson\nIcyIceBear\nWelcome to the community! You kinda answered your own question.\nGot questions about たい?\nJoin us to discuss, ask, and learn together!\nJoin the Discussion\nBunpro\nSimplifying Japanese\nOfficial Apps\nLearn More\nJoin us!\nCompany\nNews\nCareers\nAbout Us\nTestimonials\nAcknowledgements\nFor Teachers\nJapanese\nOfficial Forums\nContent Search\nReading Practice\nGrammar Library\nHiragana & Katakana\nSupport\nContact Us\nSupport & FAQ\n© 2026, Bunpro SRS.\nRead our\nTerms of Service\n,\nPrivacy Policy\nand\nCompany Overview\n.\nMade with\n❤️\nfrom Osaka.\nEnglish",
