      "sourceText": "か (JLPT N5) | Bunpro\nLoading user data...\nBunpro\nGrammar Info\nN5 Lesson 1: 12/12\nか\nQuestion marking particle\nか is also often used to mark uncertainty/doubt\nDetails\nExamples\nResources\nか\nQuestion marking particle\nDetails\nExamples\nResources\nDetails\nExamples\nResources\nReady to transform your studies?\nLearn N5 in under a month!\nTry now, no credit card required!\nTry Bunpro\nLearn More\nStructure\nPhrase +\nか\nDetails\nPart of Speech\nParticle\nWord Type\nSentence Ending Particle\nRegister\nStandard\nAbout か\nか\nis a particle that frequently comes at the end of sentences in Japanese, and carries the same meaning as a question mark in English. (It is not limited to appearing at the end of sentences, however). In addition to questions,\nか\ncan also express uncertainty about something, without strictly being a question.\nか\nregularly comes after the polite form of words, such as ～\nです\nか\n, ～ます\nか\n. However, in casual conversation,\nか\ncan be used directly after the word that the speaker is showing uncertainty about.\nBoth examples are grammatically correct, but the sentence without\nです\nmay be considered rude by some people (as it sounds too familiar/direct).\nTopics\nQuestioning Everything\nN5 Topic\nIn this Topic, we're going to learn the essentials of how questions work in Japanese and meet the question particle, か.\n3m\nSynonyms\nExpand All\nかい\nQuestion marker\nN4 Grammar\nか is the standard question particle, used at the end of sentences to form questions (e.g., どんな本が好きですか？ = 'What kind of books do you like?'). It also appears in the middle of other grammar patterns. かい is a casual, informal question particle often used by older men at the end of yes/no questions (e.g., 元気かい？ = 'Are you feeling okay?').\nAntonyms\nExpand All\nよ\nEmphasis (Sentence ending particle)\nN5 Grammar\nよ is a common sentence-ending particle used for emphasis, often indicating that the speaker is providing new information (e.g., 面白いですよ = 'It's interesting, I'm telling you!'). In contrast, か is the standard question particle, which has the opposite function, asking for information (e.g., 面白いですか？ = 'Is it interesting?').\nRelated\nExpand All\nっけ\nWhat is…again?, Was it... that... ?, Did you say...?\nN3 Grammar\nか is the standard question particle, used at the end of sentences to ask questions (e.g., どんな本が好きですか？ = 'What kind of books do you like?') and also within other grammar patterns. っけ, on the other hand, is a casual sentence-ending particle used when trying to recall something (e.g., 名前はなんだっけ？ = 'What was his name again?').\nVocab Coverage\nAll Bunpro Vocab that appears on this item.\nExpand List\nKnowledge Check\nExamples\n--:--\nSentence\nTranslation\nこれ\nは\n本\n(\nほん\n)\nです\nか\n。\nIs this a book\n?\nこれ\nは\nあなた\nの\n本\n(\nほん\n)\nです\nか\n。\nIs this your book\n?\nこれ\nも\nあなた\nの\n本\n(\nほん\n)\nです\nか\n。\nIs this also your book\n?\nこれ\nは\nペン\nです\nか\n。\nIs this a pen\n?\nこれ\nは\nいい\nです\nか\n。\nIs this good\n?\nGet more example sentences!\nPremium users get access to 12 example sentences on all Grammar Points.\nTry Bunpro\nSelf-Study Sentences\nStudy your own way!\nAdd sentences and study them alongside Bunpro sentences.\nTry Bunpro\nOnline\nIntro and 'Basic Questions in Plain Speech'\nImabi\nOverview with examples\nElon\nQuestions in polite form\nTae Kim\nOffline\n[DBJG] A Dictionary of Basic Japanese Grammar\nPage 14, 45 & 166\nGenki I 2nd Edition\nPage 43\nGenki I 3rd Edition\nPage 42\nTae Kim's Japanese Grammar Guide\nPage 96\nみんなの日本語 I\nPage 14 [CH 1]\nTrack Resources!\nBunpro tracks all of the resources you’ve visited, and offers relevant bookmarks of physical books to help with offline tracking.\nTry Bunpro\nか – Grammar Discussion\nMost Recent Replies (2 in total)\naminhnh\nDoes anyone else hear\nユウキ\nin the audio for\nこれは、ユウキさんのお母さんですか。\nsounding more like\nユイチ\n? Or is it just me?\nPablunpro\nIndeed! It sounds more\nチ\nthan\nキ\nto me too.\nGot questions about か?\nJoin us to discuss, ask, and learn together!\nJoin the Discussion\nBunpro\nSimplifying Japanese\nOfficial Apps\nLearn More\nJoin us!\nCompany\nNews\nCareers\nAbout Us\nTestimonials\nAcknowledgements\nFor Teachers\nJapanese\nOfficial Forums\nContent Search\nReading Practice\nGrammar Library\nHiragana & Katakana\nSupport\nContact Us\nSupport & FAQ\n© 2026, Bunpro SRS.\nRead our\nTerms of Service\n,\nPrivacy Policy\nand\nCompany Overview\n.\nMade with\n❤️\nfrom Osaka.\nEnglish",
